erTests.test_malformed_future_unknown_and_unsupported_queries) ... ok\ntest_model_requires_all_channels_and_contiguous_1024_samples (test_server.ServerTests.test_model_requires_all_channels_and_contiguous_1024_samples) ... ok\ntest_raw_root_rejects_gapped_source_at_startup (test_server.ServerTests.test_raw_root_rejects_gapped_source_at_startup) ... ok\ntest_raw_root_serves_an_exact_window_beyond_replay_detail (test_server.ServerTests.test_raw_root_serves_an_exact_window_beyond_replay_detail) ... ok\ntest_raw_window_accepts_decimal_boundaries_without_resampling (test_server.ServerTests.test_raw_window_accepts_decimal_boundaries_without_resampling) ... ok\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 29 tests in 12.054s\n\nOK\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa63fea137887d2befe76204e66bcef","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a09967-6f68-7451-8bfe-9712d735afe3"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_K2LuBkD0OcpdybZXIOKeNOIb","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa63fea2e7087d2b00cf32703a5ab04","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git push origin codex/incident-cohorts\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":8000,\"sandbox_permissions\":\"require_escalated\",\"justification\":\"Allow me to update PR #23 with the verified CNN-enabled main integration?\",\"prefix_rule\":[\"git\",\"push\"]}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789280232.821597,"turn_id":"01a09967-6f68-7451-8bfe-9712d735afe3"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_K2LuBkD0OcpdybZXIOKeNOIb","id":"ctco_01a09969-bdb9-7720-ba73-a38de5464e11","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789280239.033081,"turn_id":"01a09967-6f68-7451-8bfe-9712d735afe3"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.2 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"To https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet\n   02da87d..381d4df  codex/incident-cohorts -\u003e codex/incident-cohorts\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa63ff0875887d298d658d3c9a93f2b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a09967-6f68-7451-8bfe-9712d735afe3"},"summary":[{"text":"**Evaluating action plan**\n\nI realize my final answer needs concrete evidence and a solid plan. The action with the highest leverage right now is to check the v5b status, which is currently unavailable. The H100 is idle, but it's unclear if the process completed or failed. I should propose not launching the new TSLM until I've inspected v5b. Spending about 30 minutes to retrieve its status and artifacts seems reasonable, and I want to confirm I’m aligned with the overall strategy.","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Planning model deployment**\n\nI need to be cautious since if CNN is core, judges might question its role alongside TSLM. I’ll use CNN as a baseline and fallback, while OpenTSLM serves as an investigation layer. If the ModelWorkspace excludes the assistant and lists OpenTSLM, I can run both models side by side. I want to make sure CNN deployment uses the correct config and checkpoint, and emphasize not claiming results until everything's deployed. \n\nI plan to merge PR23 after review, which adds a cohort function. After that, I’ll demo it, setting a timebox of 3 hours and 45 minutes for different tasks","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa63ff74cb887d2aee04cbd4c5222e9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a09967-6f68-7451-8bfe-9712d735afe3"},"summary":[{"text":"**Evaluating action plan**\n\nI realize my final answer needs concrete evidence and a solid plan. The action with the highest leverage right now is to check the v5b status, which is currently unavailable. The H100 is idle, but it's unclear if the process completed or failed. I should propose not launching the new TSLM until I've inspected v5b. Spending about 30 minutes to retrieve its status and artifacts seems reasonable, and I want to confirm I’m aligned with the overall strategy.","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Planning model deployment**\n\nI need to be cautious since if CNN is core, judges might question its role alongside TSLM. I’ll use CNN as a baseline and fallback, while OpenTSLM serves as an investigation layer. If the ModelWorkspace excludes the assistant and lists OpenTSLM, I can run both models side by side. I want to make sure CNN deployment uses the correct config and checkpoint, and emphasize not claiming results until everything's deployed. \n\nI plan to merge PR23 after review, which adds a cohort function. After that, I’ll demo it, setting a timebox of 3 hours and 45 minutes for different tasks. This includes retrieving metrics, configuring and deploying CNN, merging PR23, and preparing the demo. Lastly, I’ll be ready to explain the business value in terms of incident triage.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"Yes, we are aligned: useful problem, TimeNet connector, trained TSLM, held-out baseline, and working evidence-linked demo.\n\nDo **not** blindly start another full training run. The H100 is currently idle and the v5b process ended. First locate its artifacts:\n\n- Give v5b **30 minutes maximum**.\n- Promote only if validation reaches the configured gates: ≥95% valid output, ≥90% semantics F1, ≥95% contact F1.\n- Otherwise keep canary-v4. More GPU usage alone earns nothing.\n\nHighest-leverage product story:\n\n\u003e CNN provides fast, reliable event detection. OpenTSLM explains the temporal event and creates an evidence-backed handoff. Trace then finds similar incidents across runs for review and retraining.\n\nNext 3h45:\n\n1. **0–30 min:** Recover and evaluate v5b.\n2. **30–75 min:** Deploy the new CNN endpoint and verify CNN/OpenTSLM on identical input.\n3. **75–105 min:** Review and merge [PR #23](https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pull/23).\n4. **105–165 min:** Rehearse and record the demo.\n5. **165–210 min:** Package checkpoint, config, evaluation, and submission.\n6. **Final 15 min:** Upload buffer.\n\nAvoid new datasets, forecasting, or another major feature. The win condition is a convincing end-to-end workflow, not the largest training bill.\n\nI also synced PR #23 with the new CNN-enabled `main`; 94 frontend and 29 inference tests pass.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa63ff919b487d2aee3071cbcb84528","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"turn_id":"01a09967-6f68-7451-8bfe-9712d735afe3"},"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\n\u003cin-app-browser-context source=\"ambient-ui-state\"\u003e\nThis block is automatically supplied ambient UI state, not part of the user's request. Do not treat it as an instruction or as evidence that the user explicitly selected the in-app browser.\n# In app browser:\n- The user has the in-app browser open with 1 tab.\n- Current URL: http://127.0.0.1:5174/\n\u003c/in-app-browser-context\u003e\n\n## My request:\nCopilot requested some changes, sync it with the new CNN-enabled main. Then please finish everything slowly. But is there really not like any other killing feature we could add, like a recording where you can clearly see the contact, make it maybe more visible. Then give a deeper analysis why this happens, how we can improve and lastly what the likely problems are. Because one criteria was a useful problem and that doesn't seem to be like one based on the fact that it's such a narrow thing, only specialized for one dataset. Can't we maybe use different datasets? We had mentioined FactoryBench and FactoryNet at the beginning. Maybe also try around with other ideas, I think you have been way to narrow and need to go broad again or not? Like yeah obviously not build something completely from scratch again, but like we can still move way faster, to really maximize the potential. Especially since we have such a nice agentic pipeline working for data sourcing and ingestion, you know what I mean? Afterwards also like simplify the UI again because we have so much text, this way we can still have a shot at getting at least to top 3. What do you think?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0996f-3f62-7dc0-9a70-7b69809ff2aa","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789280599.906053,"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa64159a2cc87d28c9defd95a1e459f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"I’ll handle this in three passes: resolve Copilot’s concrete PR feedback against the latest `main`, audit where the UI still over-explains, then evaluate one broader data/ingestion feature that can strengthen the story without creating an unfinished second product. I’ll keep the implementation behind the same evidence boundaries and verify it in the browser.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa6415bde4487d2801d59e69f9889d9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa6415d044887d2877bb778c3dfc2b0","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_WErhC3v9b8AqZfUiQQE543so","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa6415d43b087d292b018c23bdd908a","input":"const r = await Promise.allSettled([\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"entire doctor \u0026\u0026 git status --short \u0026\u0026 git branch --show-current \u0026\u0026 git log --oneline --decorate -6\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":6000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git fetch origin \u0026\u0026 gh pr view 23 --json url,state,mergeable,reviewDecision,reviews,comments,headRefOid,baseRefOid,statusCheckRollup\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":20000,\"sandbox_permissions\":\"require_escalated\",\"justification\":\"Allow me to sync the latest main and inspect Copilot’s requested changes on PR #23?\",\"prefix_rule\":[\"gh\",\"pr\"]}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh api repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/23/comments --paginate\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":24000,\"sandbox_permissions\":\"require_escalated\",\"justification\":\"Allow me to read the inline review comments on PR #23 so I can resolve them exactly?\"}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh pr list --state open --limit 20 --json number,title,headRefName,updatedAt,mergeable,url\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":10000,\"sandbox_permissions\":\"require_escalated\",\"justification\":\"Allow me to inspect open teammate work that may overlap the proposed ingestion and dataset changes?\"})\n]); for (const x of r) text(x.status===\"fulfilled\"?x.value.output:String(x.reason));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789280600.339075,"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_WErhC3v9b8AqZfUiQQE543so","id":"ctco_01a0996f-74b2-7f62-83a9-f7d1d8d6c090","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789280613.554573,"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.3 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"✓ Metadata branches: OK (no remote-tracking metadata ref found)\n\n✓ Git hooks: OK\n✓ Codex hooks: INSTALLED\n  Codex-discovered hooks: /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/.codex/hooks.json\n✓ Codex hook approval records: PRESENT\n✓ Claude Code hook config: OK\n✓ OpenCode hook config: OK\n✓ Pi hook config: OK\nNo stuck sessions found.\n?? .cursor/\n?? .factory/\n?? .gemini/\n?? .github/\n?? .opencode/\n?? .pi/\ncodex/incident-cohorts\n381d4df (HEAD -\u003e codex/incident-cohorts, origin/codex/incident-cohorts) Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into codex/incident-cohorts\nb9600ec (origin/main, origin/HEAD) merge: integrate baseline comparison and CNN endpoint\n88c537a Merge pull request #24 from ukafkasyali/bugfix/bosch-onboarding-source-root\n02da87d Simplify related incident workflow\na1163c7 (origin/bugfix/bosch-onboarding-source-root) fix(data-ingestion): complete Bosch onboarding preset\ndb014e3 (origin/baseline-comparison) feat: expose CNN inference for model comparison\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"From https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet\n   b9600ec..e817441  main       -\u003e origin/main\n{\"baseRefOid\":\"b9600ec99a1f6e49a155644ad55f372fad71bf96\",\"comments\":[],\"headRefOid\":\"381d4df51364e6c22110b4c5861ce41b1c801a25\",\"mergeable\":\"MERGEABLE\",\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"reviews\":[{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOUX3qg88AAAABNVXUDw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"copilot-pull-request-reviewer\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"### 🟡 Changes recommended\\n\\nAddress partial-cohort handling, enforce 1 kHz inputs, and exclude all candidates from the selected recording.\\n\\n*Get a fresh assessment by requesting another Copilot review.*\\n\\n\u003cdetails\u003e\\n\u003csummary\u003ePull request overview\u003c/summary\u003e\\n\\nAdds deterministic cross-run retrieval of similar raw torque windows, with comparison and cohort export for engineering review.\\n\\n**Changes:**\\n- Ranks fixed raw windows using torque-profile features.\\n- Adds comparison selection and JSON cohort export.\\n- Updates styling, documentation, tests, and demo guidance.\\n\u003c/details\u003e\\n\\n\u003cdetails\u003e\\n\u003csummary\u003eFile summaries\u003c/summary\u003e\\n\\n| File | Summary |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| `frontend/src/styles.css` | Cohort and match-list styling |\\r\\n| `frontend/src/comparison/ComparisonPanel.tsx` | Retrieval, comparison, and export UI |\\r\\n| `frontend/src/comparison/compare.ts` | Similarity signatures and ranking logic |\\r\\n| `frontend/src/comparison/compare.test.ts` | Ranking and eligibility tests |\\r\\n| `frontend/src/assistant/AssistantPanel.tsx` | Updated investigation action |\\r\\n| `frontend/README.md` | Retrieval workflow documentation |\\r\\n| `frontend/PRODUCT.md` | Product-purpose update |\\r\\n| `docs/submission/DEMO.md` | Demo flow and limitations |\\n\u003c/details\u003e\\n\\n\u003cdetails\u003e\\n\u003csummary\u003eReview details\u003c/summary\u003e\\n\\n### Files not reviewed (1)\\n\\n* **frontend/src/styles.css**: Generated file\\n\\n- **Files reviewed:** 7/8 changed files\\n- **Comments generated:** 3\\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\\n\u003c/details\u003e\\n\\n---\\n\\n💡 \u003ca href=\\\"/ukafkasyali/ysamet/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\\\" class=\\\"Link--inTextBlock\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"\u003eAdd a `code-review` agent skill\u003c/a\u003e or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. \u003ca href=\\\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\\\" class=\\\"Link--inTextBlock\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"\u003eLearn more in the docs.\u003c/a\u003e\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-09-13T06:04:59Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"83cee513c3566820758fca29d1b1981cf01a941a\"}}],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"statusCheckRollup\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pull/23\"}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"[{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/comments/3998898807\",\"pull_request_review_id\":5189784591,\"id\":3998898807,\"node_id\":\"PRRC_kwDOUX3qg87uWlp3\",\"diff_hunk\":\"@@ -48,15 +48,43 @@ export default function ComparisonPanel({ data, interval, cases, services, onEvi\\n   const [reference, setReference] = useState\u003cInterval | undefined\u003e(initial);\\n   const [suggested, setSuggested] = useState(Boolean(initial));\\n   const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false), [error, setError] = useState(''), [status, setStatus] = useState('');\\n+  const [matching, setMatching] = useState(false), [matchIssue, setMatchIssue] = useState('');\\n+  const [matches, setMatches] = useState\u003cSimilarIncident[]\u003e([]);\\n   const [joint, setJoint] = useState('');\\n   const request = useRef(0);\\n   const duration = interval.end - interval.start;\\n   useEffect(() =\u003e () =\u003e { request.current++; }, []);\\n   const options = [...new Map([{ recordingId: data.recording.id, title: 'This recording' }, { recordingId: '05-28-21-25', title: 'Original recording' }, ...cases].map(c =\u003e [c.recordingId, c])).values()];\\n+  async function recordingData(id: string) {\\n+    return id === data.recording.id ? data : id === '05-28-21-25' ? loadDemoData() : services.getReplay(id);\\n+  }\\n+  useEffect(() =\u003e {\\n+    let active = true;\\n+    const original: DemoCase = { id: 'original', title: 'Original recording', recordingId: '05-28-21-25', interval: { start: 5.787, end: 6.811 }, note: 'Fixed raw demonstration window.' };\\n+    const pool = [original, ...cases];\\n+    if (!pool.length || !services.connected) { setMatches([]); return () =\u003e { active = false; }; }\\n+    setMatching(true); setMatchIssue('');\\n+    const recordings = new Map\u003cstring, Promise\u003cDemoData\u003e\u003e();\\n+    const loadCandidate = (item: DemoCase) =\u003e {\\n+      if (!recordings.has(item.recordingId)) recordings.set(item.recordingId, recordingData(item.recordingId));\\n+      return recordings.get(item.recordingId)!.then(candidateData =\u003e ({ item, data: candidateData }));\\n+    };\\n+    Promise.allSettled(pool.map(loadCandidate)).then(results =\u003e {\\n+      if (!active) return;\\n+      const available = results.flatMap(result =\u003e result.status === 'fulfilled' ? [result.value] : []);\\n+      try {\\n+        setMatches(rankSimilarIncidents(data, interval, available).slice(0, 3));\\n+        if (available.length \u003c 2) setMatchIssue('Related recordings could not be loaded. The current investigation remains available.');\",\"path\":\"frontend/src/comparison/ComparisonPanel.tsx\",\"commit_id\":\"381d4df51364e6c22110b4c5861ce41b1c801a25\",\"original_commit_id\":\"83cee513c3566820758fca29d1b1981cf01a941a\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"Copilot\",\"id\":175728472,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-pull-request-reviewer\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"Because rejected `Promise.allSettled` results are removed at line 74, a single failed recording is invisible whenever at least two other candidates load. The UI can then rank and export a partial cohort without warning that some recordings were not considered; detect any rejected candidate rather than only `available.length \u003c 2`.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T06:04:58Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-13T06:04:59Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pull/23#discussion_r3998898807\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/23\",\"_links\":{\"self\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/comments/3998898807\"},\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pull/23#discussion_r3998898807\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/23\"}},\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/comments/3998898807/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"start_line\":null,\"original_start_line\":null,\"start_side\":null,\"line\":77,\"original_line\":77,\"side\":\"RIGHT\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"original_position\":39,\"position\":43,\"subject_type\":\"line\"},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/comments/3998898821\",\"pull_request_review_id\":5189784591,\"id\":3998898821,\"node_id\":\"PRRC_kwDOUX3qg87uWlqF\",\"diff_hunk\":\"@@ -39,6 +39,79 @@ function metrics(values: number[]) {\\n   values.forEach((v, i) =\u003e { const delta = v - mean; mean += delta / (i + 1); m2 += delta * (v - mean); min = Math.min(min, v); max = Math.max(max, v); });\\n   return { range: max - min, variability: Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, m2 / values.length)), mean };\\n }\\n+\\n+function incidentSignature(data: DemoData, interval: Interval) {\\n+  if (!rawCovers(data, interval)) throw new Error('Incident matching requires raw telemetry for the complete window.');\\n+  const sample = samples(data, interval, true);\",\"path\":\"frontend/src/comparison/compare.ts\",\"commit_id\":\"381d4df51364e6c22110b4c5861ce41b1c801a25\",\"original_commit_id\":\"83cee513c3566820758fca29d1b1981cf01a941a\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"Copilot\",\"id\":175728472,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-pull-request-reviewer\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"This path is documented and presented as matching raw 1 kHz telemetry, but `samples()` accepts any positive `recording.sampleRateHz` and this signature never enforces 1000 Hz. A replay with a different raw cadence can therefore be ranked and exported as a 1 kHz cohort. Reject non-1,000 Hz signatures here, matching the existing model-window contract.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T06:04:59Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-13T06:04:59Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pull/23#discussion_r3998898821\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/23\",\"_links\":{\"self\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/comments/3998898821\"},\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pull/23#discussion_r3998898821\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/23\"}},\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/comments/3998898821/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"start_line\":null,\"original_start_line\":null,\"start_side\":null,\"line\":45,\"original_line\":45,\"side\":\"RIGHT\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"original_position\":13,\"position\":13,\"subject_type\":\"line\"},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/comments/3998898828\",\"pull_request_review_id\":5189784591,\"id\":3998898828,\"node_id\":\"PRRC_kwDOUX3qg87uWlqM\",\"diff_hunk\":\"@@ -39,6 +39,79 @@ function metrics(values: number[]) {\\n   values.forEach((v, i) =\u003e { const delta = v - mean; mean += delta / (i + 1); m2 += delta * (v - mean); min = Math.min(min, v); max = Math.max(max, v); });\\n   return { range: max - min, variability: Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, m2 / values.length)), mean };\\n }\\n+\\n+function incidentSignature(data: DemoData, interval: Interval) {\\n+  if (!rawCovers(data, interval)) throw new Error('Incident matching requires raw telemetry for the complete window.');\\n+  const sample = samples(data, interval, true);\\n+  const features = sample.channels.flatMap(channel =\u003e {\\n+    const summary = metrics(channel.values);\\n+    let largestStep = 0;\\n+    for (let index = 1; index \u003c channel.values.length; index++) {\\n+      largestStep = Math.max(largestStep, Math.abs(channel.values[index] - channel.values[index - 1]));\\n+    }\\n+    return [summary.range, summary.variability, largestStep];\\n+  });\\n+  const strongest = sample.channels\\n+    .map(channel =\u003e ({ id: channel.id, range: metrics(channel.values).range }))\\n+    .sort((left, right) =\u003e right.range - left.range)[0]?.id;\\n+  return { features, sampleRateHz: sample.rate, samplesPerChannel: sample.times.length, strongestJoint: strongest };\\n+}\\n+\\n+function symmetricDifference(left: number, right: number) {\\n+  return Math.abs(left - right) / Math.max(Math.abs(left) + Math.abs(right), 1e-9);\\n+}\\n+\\n+export type IncidentCandidate = { item: DemoCase; data: DemoData };\\n+export type SimilarIncident = {\\n+  caseId: string;\\n+  title: string;\\n+  recordingId: string;\\n+  interval: Interval;\\n+  score: number;\\n+  strongestJoint?: string;\\n+  samplesPerChannel: number;\\n+  sourceUrl: string;\\n+  archive: string;\\n+};\\n+\\n+/**\\n+ * Rank fixed, raw incident windows by a transparent torque-profile distance.\\n+ * This is retrieval for review and cohorting, never a diagnosis or probability.\\n+ */\\n+export function rankSimilarIncidents(selectedData: DemoData, selected: Interval, candidates: IncidentCandidate[]): SimilarIncident[] {\\n+  const selectedSignature = incidentSignature(selectedData, selected);\\n+  const selectedDuration = selected.end - selected.start;\\n+  const ranked: SimilarIncident[] = [];\\n+  for (const candidate of candidates) {\\n+    const interval = candidate.item.interval;\\n+    if (candidate.data.recording.id === selectedData.recording.id\\n+      \u0026\u0026 Math.abs(interval.start - selected.start) \u003c 1e-9\\n+      \u0026\u0026 Math.abs(interval.end - selected.end) \u003c 1e-9) continue;\",\"path\":\"frontend/src/comparison/compare.ts\",\"commit_id\":\"381d4df51364e6c22110b4c5861ce41b1c801a25\",\"original_commit_id\":\"83cee513c3566820758fca29d1b1981cf01a941a\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"Copilot\",\"id\":175728472,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-pull-request-reviewer\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"This only excludes the exact selected interval, so a selected case such as `03-15-12-53` can rank the `free` case from that same recording and present/export it under “across runs.” Skip every candidate from the selected recording here; same-recording manual comparisons remain available in the reference editor below.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T06:04:59Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-13T06:04:59Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pull/23#discussion_r3998898828\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/23\",\"_links\":{\"self\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/comments/3998898828\"},\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pull/23#discussion_r3998898828\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/23\"}},\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pulls/comments/3998898828/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"start_line\":87,\"original_start_line\":87,\"start_side\":\"RIGHT\",\"line\":89,\"original_line\":89,\"side\":\"RIGHT\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"original_position\":57,\"position\":57,\"subject_type\":\"line\"}]","type":"input_text"},{"text":"[{\"headRefName\":\"codex/incident-cohorts\",\"mergeable\":\"UNKNOWN\",\"number\":23,\"title\":\"Turn incident analysis into reusable failure cohorts\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-13T06:17:20Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pull/23\"},{\"headRefName\":\"codex/source-ingestion-integration\",\"mergeable\":\"UNKNOWN\",\"number\":19,\"title\":\"Integrate approved dataset sourcing with one-shot ingestion\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-13T06:11:48Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pull/19\"}]\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa64167953c87d29fd73be1373d642b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_1CnSJandW9cQaTjA7DPPArrd","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa6416dffdc87d28ac4dd83048a726f","input":"const r = await Promise.allSettled([\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git log --oneline --decorate b9600ec..origin/main \u0026\u0026 git diff --stat b9600ec..origin/main\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":8000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '35,125p' frontend/src/comparison/ComparisonPanel.tsx; sed -n '35,125p' frontend/src/comparison/compare.ts; sed -n '70,150p' frontend/src/comparison/compare.test.ts\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":16000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git diff --stat origin/main...HEAD \u0026\u0026 git diff --check\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":5000})\n]); for (const x of r) text(x.status===\"fulfilled\"?x.value.output:String(x.reason));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789280614.160291,"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_1CnSJandW9cQaTjA7DPPArrd","id":"ctco_01a0996f-9d7e-7460-8ade-d7466d44bc8d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789280623.998728,"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"e817441 (origin/main, origin/HEAD) Merge pull request #25 from ukafkasyali/bugfix/bosch-onboarding-source-root\nf52e12b fix(data-ingestion): keep TimeNet cache within onboarding job\n data_ingestion/src/dataset_profiler/onboarding/presets.py | 5 ++++-\n 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"      \u003cpath d={`M576,230 L576,214 L${rx},${ry}`} className=\"graph-leader reference-leader\"/\u003e\n      \u003ccircle cx={rx} cy={ry} r=\"5\" className=\"graph-point reference-point\"/\u003e\n      \u003ccircle cx={sx} cy={sy} r=\"5\" className=\"graph-point selected-point\"/\u003e\n    \u003c/svg\u003e\n    \u003cdiv className=\"graph-callout reference-callout\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReference · sampled peak\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cspan\u003e{signed(referencePeak.value)} Nm at {fixed(referencePeak.time)} s\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003cdiv className=\"comparison-axis\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e0 ms\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan\u003eTime from each window’s start\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan\u003e{Math.round(length * 1000)} ms\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eCircles mark each curve’s largest absolute sampled torque, with its signed value. {result.resolution === 'raw' ? 'Raw samples.' : 'Overview samples; brief peaks may be missed.'} Peaks are measurements, not detected collisions. Motion phases may differ.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e;\n}\nexport default function ComparisonPanel({ data, interval, cases, services, onEvidence }: Props) {\n  const [referenceData, setReferenceData] = useState(data);\n  const [referenceId, setReferenceId] = useState(data.recording.id);\n  const initial = suggestReference(data, interval);\n  const [start, setStart] = useState(initial ? fixed(initial.start) : '');\n  const [reference, setReference] = useState\u003cInterval | undefined\u003e();\n  const [suggested, setSuggested] = useState(Boolean(initial));\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false), [error, setError] = useState(''), [status, setStatus] = useState('');\n  const [matching, setMatching] = useState(false), [matchIssue, setMatchIssue] = useState('');\n  const [matches, setMatches] = useState\u003cSimilarIncident[]\u003e([]);\n  const [joint, setJoint] = useState('');\n  const request = useRef(0);\n  const duration = interval.end - interval.start;\n  useEffect(() =\u003e () =\u003e { request.current++; }, []);\n  const options = [...new Map([{ recordingId: data.recording.id, title: 'This recording' }, { recordingId: '05-28-21-25', title: 'Original recording' }, ...cases].map(c =\u003e [c.recordingId, c])).values()];\n  async function recordingData(id: string) {\n    return id === data.recording.id ? data : id === '05-28-21-25' ? loadDemoData() : services.getReplay(id);\n  }\n  useEffect(() =\u003e {\n    let active = true;\n    const original: DemoCase = { id: 'original', title: 'Original recording', recordingId: '05-28-21-25', interval: { start: 5.787, end: 6.811 }, note: 'Fixed raw demonstration window.' };\n    const pool = [original, ...cases];\n    if (!pool.length || !services.connected) { setMatches([]); return () =\u003e { active = false; }; }\n    setMatching(true); setMatchIssue('');\n    const recordings = new Map\u003cstring, Promise\u003cDemoData\u003e\u003e();\n    const loadCandidate = (item: DemoCase) =\u003e {\n      if (!recordings.has(item.recordingId)) recordings.set(item.recordingId, recordingData(item.recordingId));\n      return recordings.get(item.recordingId)!.then(candidateData =\u003e ({ item, data: candidateData }));\n    };\n    Promise.allSettled(pool.map(loadCandidate)).then(results =\u003e {\n      if (!active) return;\n      const available = results.flatMap(result =\u003e result.status === 'fulfilled' ? [result.value] : []);\n      try {\n        setMatches(rankSimilarIncidents(data, interval, available).slice(0, 3));\n        if (available.length \u003c 2) setMatchIssue('Related recordings could not be loaded. The current investigation remains available.');\n      } catch (cause) {\n        setMatches([]);\n        setMatchIssue(cause instanceof Error \u0026\u0026 cause.message.includes('raw telemetry')\n          ? 'This interval only has overview data. Choose a named demo case with a complete 1.024 s raw window.'\n          : cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : 'Incident matching is unavailable.');\n      } finally { setMatching(false); }\n    });\n    return () =\u003e { active = false; };\n  }, [cases, data, interval.start, interval.end, services]);\n  async function chooseRecording(id: string) {\n    const version = ++request.current; setReferenceId(id); setLoading(true); setError(''); setReference(undefined); setStatus('');\n    try {\n      const next = await recordingData(id);\n      if (version !== request.current) return;\n      if (next.recording.id !== id) throw new Error('The service returned a different recording.');\n      setReferenceData(next);\n      const suggestion = id === data.recording.id ? suggestReference(next, interval) : undefined;\n      setReference(suggestion); setStart(suggestion ? fixed(suggestion.start) : ''); setSuggested(Boolean(suggestion));\n    } catch (e) { if (version === request.current) setError(e instanceof Error ? e.message : 'Reference could not load. Choose it again to retry.'); }\n    finally { if (version === request.current) setLoading(false); }\n  }\n  async function chooseMatch(match: SimilarIncident) {\n    const version = ++request.current; setReferenceId(match.recordingId); setLoading(true); setError(''); setReference(undefined); setStatus('');\n    try {\n      const next = await recordingData(match.recordingId);\n      if (version !== request.current) return;\n      if (next.recording.id !== match.recordingId) throw new Error('The service returned a different recording.');\n      setReferenceData(next); setReference({ ...match.interval }); setStart(fixed(match.interval.start)); setSuggested(false);\n    } catch (cause) { if (version === request.current) setError(cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : 'Related incident could not load.'); }\n    finally { if (version === request.current) setLoading(false); }\n  }\n  const computed = useMemo(() =\u003e {\n    if (!reference || loading || !start.trim() || Number(start) !== reference.start) return {};\n    try { return { result: compareWindows(data, interval, referenceData, reference) }; }\n    catch (e) { return { issue: e instanceof Error ? e.message : 'Comparison unavailable.' }; }\n  }, [data, interval, referenceData, reference, loading, start]);\n  const result = computed.result;\n  const selectedJoint = result?.joints.find(j =\u003e j.id === joint) ?? result?.joints[0];\n  function apply() {\n    if (!start.trim() || loading || referenceData.recording.id !== referenceId) { setError('Load a reference recording and enter its start time.'); return; }\n    const value = Number(start); setReference({ start: value, end: Math.round((value + duration) * 1e6) / 1e6 }); setSuggested(false); setError(''); setStatus('');\n  }\n  function exportComparison() {\n    if (!result) return;\n    const content = { ...comparisonReport(result), referenceSelection: suggested ? 'Suggested earlier annotation-free window with 0.5 s marker margin; not verified normal.' : 'User-selected reference; not verified normal.' };\n    const url = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([JSON.stringify(content, null, 2) + '\\n'], { type: 'application/json' }));\n    const link = document.createElement('a'); link.href = url; link.download = `trace-comparison-${data.recording.id}.json`; link.click();\n    setTimeout(() =\u003e URL.revokeObjectURL(url), 1000); setStatus('Comparison report downloaded.');\n  return { times, channels, rate };\n}\nfunction metrics(values: number[]) {\n  let mean = 0, m2 = 0, min = Infinity, max = -Infinity;\n  values.forEach((v, i) =\u003e { const delta = v - mean; mean += delta / (i + 1); m2 += delta * (v - mean); min = Math.min(min, v); max = Math.max(max, v); });\n  return { range: max - min, variability: Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, m2 / values.length)), mean };\n}\n\nfunction incidentSignature(data: DemoData, interval: Interval) {\n  if (!rawCovers(data, interval)) throw new Error('Incident matching requires raw telemetry for the complete window.');\n  const sample = samples(data, interval, true);\n  const features = sample.channels.flatMap(channel =\u003e {\n    const summary = metrics(channel.values);\n    let largestStep = 0;\n    for (let index = 1; index \u003c channel.values.length; index++) {\n      largestStep = Math.max(largestStep, Math.abs(channel.values[index] - channel.values[index - 1]));\n    }\n    return [summary.range, summary.variability, largestStep];\n  });\n  const strongest = sample.channels\n    .map(channel =\u003e ({ id: channel.id, range: metrics(channel.values).range }))\n    .sort((left, right) =\u003e right.range - left.range)[0]?.id;\n  return { features, sampleRateHz: sample.rate, samplesPerChannel: sample.times.length, strongestJoint: strongest };\n}\n\nfunction symmetricDifference(left: number, right: number) {\n  return Math.abs(left - right) / Math.max(Math.abs(left) + Math.abs(right), 1e-9);\n}\n\nexport type IncidentCandidate = { item: DemoCase; data: DemoData };\nexport type SimilarIncident = {\n  caseId: string;\n  title: string;\n  recordingId: string;\n  interval: Interval;\n  score: number;\n  strongestJoint?: string;\n  samplesPerChannel: number;\n  sourceUrl: string;\n  archive: string;\n};\n\n/**\n * Rank fixed, raw incident windows by a transparent torque-profile distance.\n * This is retrieval for review and cohorting, never a diagnosis or probability.\n */\nexport function rankSimilarIncidents(selectedData: DemoData, selected: Interval, candidates: IncidentCandidate[]): SimilarIncident[] {\n  const selectedSignature = incidentSignature(selectedData, selected);\n  const selectedDuration = selected.end - selected.start;\n  const ranked: SimilarIncident[] = [];\n  for (const candidate of candidates) {\n    const interval = candidate.item.interval;\n    if (candidate.data.recording.id === selectedData.recording.id\n      \u0026\u0026 Math.abs(interval.start - selected.start) \u003c 1e-9\n      \u0026\u0026 Math.abs(interval.end - selected.end) \u003c 1e-9) continue;\n    if (Math.abs((interval.end - interval.start) - selectedDuration) \u003e 1e-7) continue;\n    try {\n      const signature = incidentSignature(candidate.data, interval);\n      if (signature.sampleRateHz !== selectedSignature.sampleRateHz\n        || signature.samplesPerChannel !== selectedSignature.samplesPerChannel) continue;\n      const distance = signature.features.reduce(\n        (total, value, index) =\u003e total + symmetricDifference(value, selectedSignature.features[index]), 0,\n      ) / signature.features.length;\n      ranked.push({\n        caseId: candidate.item.id,\n        title: candidate.item.title,\n        recordingId: candidate.data.recording.id,\n        interval: { ...interval },\n        score: Math.max(0, Math.min(1, 1 - distance)),\n        strongestJoint: signature.strongestJoint,\n        samplesPerChannel: signature.samplesPerChannel,\n        sourceUrl: candidate.data.recording.sourceUrl,\n        archive: candidate.data.recording.archive,\n      });\n    } catch {\n      // A candidate without complete raw evidence is not eligible for the cohort.\n    }\n  }\n  return ranked.sort((left, right) =\u003e right.score - left.score || left.recordingId.localeCompare(right.recordingId));\n}\nexport function compareWindows(selectedData: DemoData, selected: Interval, referenceData: DemoData, reference: Interval) {\n  if (Math.abs((selected.end - selected.start) - (reference.end - reference.start)) \u003e 1e-7) throw new Error('Use equal-duration windows for this comparison.');\n  if (selectedData.recording.id === referenceData.recording.id \u0026\u0026 selected.start \u003c reference.end \u0026\u0026 reference.start \u003c selected.end) throw new Error('Choose a reference that does not overlap the selected incident.');\n  const raw = rawCovers(selectedData, selected) \u0026\u0026 rawCovers(referenceData, reference);\n  const a = samples(selectedData, selected, raw), b = samples(referenceData, reference, raw);\n  if (a.rate !== b.rate) throw new Error('These recordings have different sample rates. Comparison does not resample signals.');\n  const joints = a.channels.map((c, i) =\u003e {\n    const current = metrics(c.values), baseline = metrics(b.channels[i].values);\n    return { id: c.id, name: c.name, selected: current, reference: baseline,\n      rangeDelta: current.range - baseline.range, variabilityDelta: current.variability - baseline.variability,\n      meanDelta: current.mean - baseline.mean };\n    expect(matches[0]).toMatchObject({ score:1, strongestJoint:'joint_7', samplesPerChannel:1024 });\n    expect(matches[1].score).toBeLessThan(matches[0].score);\n  });\n  it('excludes the selected window and candidates without complete raw evidence', () =\u003e {\n    const selected = fixture('selected');\n    const unavailable = fixture('unavailable'); unavailable.detail.endSeconds = 1.5;\n    const matches = rankSimilarIncidents(selected, current, [\n      { item: { id:'same', title:'Same', recordingId:'selected', interval:current, note:'' }, data:selected },\n      { item: { id:'unavailable', title:'Unavailable', recordingId:'unavailable', interval:reference, note:'' }, data:unavailable },\n    ]);\n    expect(matches).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":" docs/submission/DEMO.md                     | 15 +++---\n frontend/PRODUCT.md                         |  2 +-\n frontend/README.md                          | 12 +++--\n frontend/src/assistant/AssistantPanel.tsx   |  2 +-\n frontend/src/comparison/ComparisonPanel.tsx | 84 +++++++++++++++++++++++++----\n frontend/src/comparison/compare.test.ts     | 23 +++++++-\n frontend/src/comparison/compare.ts          | 75 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n frontend/src/styles.css                     | 20 +++++++\n 8 files changed, 208 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa64173344887d29a01c9c2cfea42b1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_yhgtxpxZcTlklKEevecSBWrb","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa641734de487d28114cb328ab5ece6","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git merge origin/main\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":8000,\"sandbox_permissions\":\"require_escalated\",\"justification\":\"Allow me to sync PR #23 with the newest ingestion fix on main before applying Copilot’s changes?\",\"prefix_rule\":[\"git\",\"merge\"]}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789280624.490698,"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_yhgtxpxZcTlklKEevecSBWrb","id":"ctco_01a0996f-b522-7312-9552-52ac91b4c933","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789280630.050831,"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.0 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"Merge made by the 'ort' strategy.\n data_ingestion/src/dataset_profiler/onboarding/presets.py | 5 ++++-\n 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa64178bc9c87d295cf5f63eb14ce29","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"summary":[{"text":"**Simplifying app features**\n\nI'm considering whether we should inspect the app's updated main features through the browser after syncing. The local server's hot updates branch includes a lot of new information. The user wants a simplified version because there's too much text. I need to be cautious not to oversimplify. \n\nOne feature that stands out is the \"incident focus mode,\" which could automatically show predicted onset on the robot and narrow down two","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_xYkUBuIopLxrw0cYNIKdQRsn","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa6417fd65887d29b683116e3b28d56","input":"const r = await tools.web__run({search_query:[\n  {q:\"FactoryBench dataset industrial time series official GitHub FactoryBench\"},\n  {q:\"FactoryNet dataset industrial manufacturing time series official\"},\n  {q:\"FactoryBench Aionic TimeNet factory dataset\"}\n],\"response_length\":\"long\"}); text(JSON.stringify(r));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789280630.313874,"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_xYkUBuIopLxrw0cYNIKdQRsn","id":"ctco_01a0996f-e70f-7d81-b1fe-dcd3d1df7e52","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789280642.831309,"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\"FactoryBench/README.md at main · Forgis-Labs/FactoryBench · GitHub (https://github.com/Forgis-Labs/FactoryBench/blob/main/README.md)\\nciteturn10search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Python library and CLI for evaluating language models on the FactoryBench benchmark of industrial-machine reasoning across four causal levels (state / intervention / counterfactual / decision). ...     factorybench info                                            # version, dataset revision, cache, providers, prices ...   * Prompt caching on the Anthropic adapter -- each FactoryBench item has a unique time-series body, and the shared prefix per level (description + acronym mapping) is well below the 2K / 4K minimum cacheable prefix on Sonnet / Opus.\\n\\nEdit and raw actions\\n\\n# factorybench\\n\\nPython library and CLI for evaluating language models on the FactoryBench benchmark of industrial-machine reasoning across four causal levels (state / intervention / counterfactual / decision). Dataset: `FactoryBench/FactoryBench` on the Hugging Face Hub.\\n\\nWhat's included: dataset loader, prompt renderer, deterministic scorer for Levels 1-3, opt-in LLM-as-judge ensemble for Level 4 (with cache + Fleiss' kappa), built-in OpenAI / Anthropic / DeepSeek adapters, cost preview, model comparison, and a CLI covering the full evaluate / export / score / compare workflow. See `CHANGELOG.md` for what's landed.\\n\\n## Install\\n    \\n    pip install -e .                       # base install (mock model only)\\n    pip install -e \\\".[openai]\\\"             # adds OpenAI / DeepSeek (gpt-*, deepseek-*)\\n    pip install -e \\\".[anthropic]\\\"          # adds Anthropic (claude-*)\\n    pip install -e \\\".[all]\\\"                # everything\\n    pip install -e \\\".[dev]\\\"                # pytest for running the test suite\\n\\nThe base install includes `tiktoken` for tiktoken-counted cost previews; if it ever fails to import (air-gapped environments, lazy BPE-download failure on first use), the library falls back to a `len(text) / 4` heuristic and surfaces that in the preview output.\\n\\nPython 3.10+.\\n\\n### Provider credentials\\n\\nSet whichever provider keys you need before running:\\n    \\n    # bash / zsh\\n    export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\\n    export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...\\n    export DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=...\\n    \\n    # PowerShell\\n    $env:OPENAI_API_KEY    = 'sk-...'\\n    $env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = 'sk-ant-...'\\n    $env:DEEPSEEK_API_KEY  = '...'\\n\\n`factorybench info` shows which providers are configured and prints the exact `export` / `$env:` line for any that are missing. The library reads keys from the environment only -- it does not auto-load `.env` files. If you keep keys in a `.env`, source it yourself (`source .env` in bash, or `python-dotenv` in your own scripts) before invoking `factorybench` -- this matches the behavior of the underlying OpenAI / Anthropic SDKs and avoids surprising configuration.\\n\\n## Quick start (Python)\\n    \\n    from factorybench import register_model, evaluate\\n    \\n    @register_model(\\\"dummy\\\")\\n    class Dummy:\\n        def predict(self, prompt: str) -\u003e str:\\n            return \\\"0\\\"\\n    \\n    result = evaluate(model=\\\"dummy\\\", level=\\\"L1\\\", max_items=20)\\n    print(result.score)\\n    print(result.by_level())\\n    print(result.by_answer_format())\\n    df = result.to_dataframe()\\n\\n`evaluate(...)` accepts:\\n\\n  * `model`: a registered model name, a built-in provider spec (`\\\"mock\\\"`, `\\\"gpt-5.1\\\"`, `\\\"claude-sonnet-4.6\\\"`, `\\\"deepseek-chat\\\"`, ...), or any object with `predict(prompt) -\u003e str` (optionally `predict_batch(prompts) -\u003e list[str]`).\\n  * `level`: `\\\"L1\\\" | \\\"L2\\\" | \\\"L3\\\" | \\\"all\\\"` (L4 is rejected — needs a judge ensemble).\\n  * `split`: `\\\"test\\\"` (default), `\\\"validation\\\"`, `\\\"train\\\"`, or `\\\"mini\\\"` (50 items per level).\\n  * `max_items`: cap per level (useful for smoke tests).\\n  * `progress`: show a tqdm bar (default `True`).\\n\\n## CLI\\n    \\n    factorybench info                                            # version, dataset revision, cache, providers, prices\\n    factorybench info --json                                     # machine-readable (paste into bug reports)\\n    factorybench cache stats                                     # judge cache size + age\\n    factorybench cache clear -y                                  # wipe the judge cache\\n    factorybench prices list                                     # bundled price table + version stamp\\n    factorybench prices source                                   # show where prices are loaded from\\n    factorybench list models                                     # registered + built-in\\n    factorybench list levels                                     # item counts per level\\n    factorybench list templates --level L2                       # templates within a level\\n    \\n    # online evaluation against a provider\\n    factorybench evaluate --model claude-sonnet-4.6 --split mini\\n    factorybench evaluate --model gpt-5.1 --level L2 --max-items 50\\n    factorybench evaluate --model mock --level all --split mini  # no API needed\\n    \\n    # user-registered model from a script file\\n    factorybench evaluate --model my-model --import ./my_models.py --split mini\\n    \\n    # offline workflow (run inference yourself)\\n    factorybench export --level L2 --output prompts.jsonl\\n    # ... run your model over prompts.jsonl, writing {item_id, prediction} JSONL ...\\n    factorybench score --predictions predictions.jsonl --level L2 --output scores.json\\n\\nBuilt-in provider specs map to:\\n\\nPattern  | Adapter  | Required env var\\n--- | --- | ---\\n`mock`  | Canned-response (no API)  | --\\n`gpt-*`  | OpenAI chat completions  | `OPENAI_API_KEY`\\n`claude-*`  | Anthropic Messages API  | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`\\n`deepseek-*`  | DeepSeek (OpenAI-compatible)  | `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`\\n\\n    factorybench evaluate --model my-model --level L4 --judges deepseek-v3.2\\n\\nThe CLI prechecks required env vars (`OPENAI_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`) before any call is made -- if a key is missing, it exits with a clean error naming exactly which variable to set.\\n\\nEach L4 item's votes and the aggregate (median) are preserved in the saved JSON, and the result reports inter-judge agreement (Fleiss' kappa):\\n    \\n    result.l4_items()       # ItemResults that went through the panel\\n    result.fleiss_kappa()   # agreement across all L4 items\\n    result.judge_mode()     # 'paper-default' | 'single-judge' | 'custom'\\n\\nJudge calls are cached at `~/.cache/factorybench/judges/`, keyed on `(item_id, prediction_hash, judge_model, rubric_version)`. Re-runs with the same predictions and judge set make zero new API calls.\\n\\nJudges run in parallel by default (one thread per judge in the panel, capped at 8). Override with `--judge-concurrency N` -- set `1` to force sequential, or raise it for very large ensembles. Each judge is a different provider, so they don't share rate limits and parallelism is a free ~3x speedup on the paper-default ensemble.\\n\\nBy default, `--level all` skips L4 unless `--judges` is also given.\\n\\n    factorybench evaluate --model my-model --level L4 --judges paper-default \\\\\\n        --judge-cache-only\\n\\nSame three options are available on the Python API:\\n    \\n    result = fb.evaluate(\\n        model=\\\"gpt-5.1\\\",\\n        level=\\\"L4\\\",\\n        judges=\\\"paper-default\\\",\\n        concurrency=8,\\n        resume_from=\\\"results/my-run.json\\\",\\n        judge_cache_only=False,\\n    )\\n\\n## Cost preview\\n\\nBefore kicking off a paid run, get an order-of-magnitude estimate:\\n    \\n    # Standalone preview (no API calls).\\n    factorybench cost --model claude-sonnet-4.6 --level L4 --judges paper-default\\n    \\n    # evaluate --dry-run: same preview, exits 0 without running.\\n    factorybench evaluate --model claude-sonnet-4.6 --level L4 \\\\\\n        --judges paper-default --dry-run\\n    \\n    # Any L4 run (or run with estimated total \u003e $1) auto-prompts. Skip with --yes\\n    # in CI / scripted runs.\\n    factorybench evaluate --model claude-sonnet-4.6 --level L4 --judges paper-default\\n    # \u003e Continue? [y/N]:\\n    \\n    factorybench evaluate --model claude-sonnet-4.6 --level L4 --judges paper-default --yes\\n## Comparing models\\n\\nAfter running several models on the same split, drop a model x level table into your paper:\\n    \\n    from factorybench import evaluate, compare\\n    \\n    results = {\\n        \\\"gpt-5.1\\\":            evaluate(model=\\\"gpt-5.1\\\",           split=\\\"mini\\\"),\\n        \\\"claude-sonnet-4.6\\\":  evaluate(model=\\\"claude-sonnet-4.6\\\", split=\\\"mini\\\"),\\n        \\\"my-model\\\":           evaluate(model=\\\"my-model\\\",          split=\\\"mini\\\"),\\n    }\\n    comp = compare(results)\\n    print(comp.to_markdown())                # paste into a draft\\n    print(comp.to_latex(booktabs=True))      # paste into LaTeX\\n    comp.to_dataframe()                      # long-form pandas\\n\\nBest-per-row is bolded automatically (`bold_best=False` to disable). Absent or unscored levels render as `--`. `compare()` also accepts a dict of `model_name -\u003e path-to-result.json` (loaded for you), or just an iterable of paths (column names come from file stems).\\n\\nFrom the CLI:\\n    \\n    factorybench compare results/m0.json results/m1.json results/m2.json\\n    factorybench compare results/*.json --format latex --output table.tex\\n    factorybench compare m0.json m1.json --name gpt-5.1 --name claude-sonnet-4.6\\n\\n## What's intentionally missing\\n\\n  * Leaderboard `submit` subcommand (needs a backend).\\n  * Auto-fetched price table; the bundled snapshot is updated by hand. Use `set_price()`, `FB_PRICES`, or drop a file at `~/.config/factorybench/prices.json` to override.\\n  * Heatmap renderer on `Comparison` -- markdown/latex/json cover the paper use case.\\n  * Prompt caching on the Anthropic adapter -- each FactoryBench item has a unique time-series body, and the shared prefix per level (description + acronym mapping) is well below the 2K / 4K minimum cacheable prefix on Sonnet / Opus. Adding `cache_control` here would write entries that are never read.\\n\\n## Contributing\\n\\nSee CONTRIBUTING.md for dev setup, testing, and the bar for PRs. Bug reports should include the output of `factorybench info --json`.\\n\\n## Citation\\n\\nIf you use FactoryBench in academic work, please cite the paper:\\n    \\n    @article{factorybench2026,\\n      title   = {FactoryBench: Evaluating Industrial Machine Understanding},\\n      author  = {Merzouki, Yanis and Izquierdo, Coral and Ignuta-Ciuncanu, Matei and G{\\\\'o}mez-Bracamonte, Marcos and Maggioni, Riccardo and Lombardi, Alessandro and Mazzoleni, Camilla and Martelli, Federico and G{\\\\\\\"u}nther, Bal{\\\\'a}zs and Petersen, Jonas and Petersen, Philipp},\\n      journal = {arXiv preprint arXiv:2605.07675},\\n      year    = {2026}\\n    }\\n\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nGitHub - blobfishai/factory-agent-simulation: Executable Oracle-shaped manufacturing ERP world and FactoryBench-100 benchmark · GitHub (https://github.com/blobfishai/factory-agent-simulation)\\nciteturn10search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; benchmark/factorybench100  | benchmark/factorybench100  |    | ...   * Hugging Face: https://huggingface.co/datasets/SamuelChien821/factorybench-100 ... Dataset content is CC BY 4.0; see `LICENSE` and `LICENSE-DATA`.\\n\\nblobfishai / factory-agent-simulation Public\\n\\n  * Notifications You must be signed in to change notification settings\\n  * Fork 0\\n  * Star\\n\\n  * Code\\n  * Issues 0\\n  * Pull requests 0\\n  * Actions\\n  * Projects\\n  * Security and quality 0\\n  * Insights\\n\\nAdditional navigation options\\n\\nmain\\n\\nBranchesTags\\n\\n[Input: Go to file]\\n\\nGo to file\\n\\nCode\\n\\nOpen more actions menu\\n\\n## Latest commit\\n\\n \\n\\n## History\\n\\n12 Commits\\n\\n## Folders and files\\n\\nName  | Name  | Last commit message  | Last commit date\\n--- | --- | --- | ---\\nbenchmark/factorybench100  | benchmark/factorybench100  |    |  \\nfactorybench  | factorybench  |    |  \\nmodel_runs  | model_runs  |    |  \\ntests  | tests  |    |  \\n.gitignore  | .gitignore  |    |  \\nLICENSE  | LICENSE  |    |  \\nLICENSE-DATA  | LICENSE-DATA  |    |  \\nNOTICE  | NOTICE  |    |  \\nREADME.md  | README.md  |    |  \\npyproject.toml  | pyproject.toml  |    |  \\nuv.lock  | uv.lock  |    |  \\n\\n# Factory Agent Simulation\\n\\nThis repository contains the executable FactoryBench-100 world and release: 100 distinct long-horizon enterprise workflows across 20 manufacturing, supply, procurement, receiving, payables, quality, maintenance, project, field-service, compliance, and close-control families.\\n\\nThe world is clean-room and synthetic. Every Oracle tool maps one-to-one to a documented Oracle Fusion Cloud 26a REST operation, and every collaboration tool maps to a documented Gmail v1, Drive v3, Sheets v4, or Slack Web API operation. It ships no Oracle code, proprietary UI, or customer data.\\n\\n## What is public\\n\\n  * An isolated multi-system SQLite starting state for every task\\n  * 94 typed, source-pinned operations across Oracle Fusion, Gmail, Drive, Sheets, Slack, and the benchmark harness\\nThey persist as actual state and fail the task-specific payload or readback criteria; the API never reveals a hidden approved value.\\n\\n## Full-suite model run\\n\\nOnly version-pinned full-suite model runs are eligible for the public leaderboard. Each accepted manifest publishes coverage, aggregate and task-level FactoryScores, exceptions, tool calls, cost, trajectories, verifier verdicts, reward records, and any disclosed runtime overlay. Results are imported directly from Harbor; they are never reconstructed from oracle traces or carried forward across a benchmark version change.\\n\\n## Run locally\\n\\nPython 3.12 or newer is required.\\n    \\n    python3.12 -m pip install -e '.[dev]'\\n    python3.12 -m pytest -q\\n    python3.12 -m factorybench.evaluation\\n    python3.12 -m factorybench.release\\n\\nRun one task through the actual stdio MCP server (the `factorybench-server` name remains as a compatibility alias):\\n    \\n    factorybench-mcp \\\\\\n      --task factorybench-001 \\\\\\n      --db /tmp/factorybench-001.db \\\\\\n      --fresh\\n\\nThe server accepts `initialize`, `tools/list`, and `tools/call` JSON-RPC messages on stdin. The generated Harbor tasks also expose a terminal-friendly `tool` CLI. Inside Harbor, the agent container has no database, runtime, verifier, or gold state; it can reach the private ERP sidecar only through the declared tools. The checked-in `benchmark/factorybench100/environment/mcp.json` can be copied directly into Codex, Claude Desktop, or another stdio MCP client.\\n\\n## Release outputs\\n\\nThe checked-in release is under `benchmark/factorybench100`:\\n\\n  * `tasks/` — complete task specifications\\n  * `assets/` — 2,800 agent-visible source artifacts\\n  * `state/` — exact evaluator starting state, outside the agent-visible asset room\\n  * `environment/` — SQLite schema and tool contracts\\n  * `trajectories/` — replayed oracle tool traces and state diffs\\n  * `verifiers/contracts/` — sealed deterministic verifier contracts\\n  * `reports/` — build and qualification evidence\\n  * `huggingface/` — dataset-card and JSONL upload tree\\n  * `harbor/` — 100 portable Harbor 1.4 tasks\\n  * `website-data.json` — Blobfish benchmark explorer payload\\n\\n## Design lineage\\n\\nThe workflow data shape is grounded in production-style operations: evidence split across ERP, email, Drive, Sheets, Slack, vendor PDFs, and technical files; explicit approvals; strict transaction rollback; lot and serial inventory; amount reconciliation; write-back; and stakeholder communication. Public presentation and distribution take inspiration from Mercor APEX, Archipelago, Enterprise-Bench, and ERP-Bench. FactoryBench tasks, records, tools, and verifiers are independently authored.\\n\\n## Links\\n\\n  * Website: https://blobfish.ai/benchmarks/factorybench-100\\n  * Hugging Face: https://huggingface.co/datasets/SamuelChien821/factorybench-100\\n  * Harbor: https://hub.harborframework.com/datasets/blobfishai/factorybench-100/latest\\n\\nCode is Apache-2.0. Dataset content is CC BY 4.0; see `LICENSE` and `LICENSE-DATA`.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nREADME.md · FactoryBench/FactoryBench at main (https://huggingface.co/datasets/FactoryBench/FactoryBench/blob/main/README.md)\\nciteturn10search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Tags: robotics industrial time-series causal-reasoning benchmark machine-understanding ... If you use FactoryBench, please cite the dataset and the two upstream open-source datasets it incorporates (AURSAD and voraus-AD):\\n\\n# Datasets:\\n\\n* * *\\n\\nFactoryBench\\n\\n/\\n\\nFactoryBench\\n\\nlike [Button: 2]\\n\\nTasks: Question Answering Time Series Forecasting\\n\\nLanguages: English\\n\\nSize: 10K\u003cn\u003c100K\\n\\nArXiv:\\n\\narxiv: 2202.03211\\n\\narxiv: 2311.04153\\n\\nTags: robotics industrial time-series causal-reasoning benchmark machine-understanding\\n\\nLicense:\\n\\ncc-by-4.0\\n\\nDataset card Files xet Community\\n\\nmain\\n\\nFactoryBench / README.md\\n\\nImage: FactoryBench's picture\\n\\nFactoryBench\\n\\nREADME: correct license section to CC BY 4.0 (matches YAML frontmatter)\\n\\ne769902 verified\\n\\npreview code\\n\\n|\\n\\nRaw\\n\\nDownload with hf CLI\\n\\nCopy download link\\n\\nHistory Blame Contribute Delete\\n\\nSafe\\n\\n10 kB\\n\\nmetadata\\n    \\n    license: cc-by-4.0\\n    language:\\n      - en\\n    task_categories:\\n      - question-answering\\n      - time-series-forecasting\\n    tags:\\n      - robotics\\n      - industrial\\n      - time-series\\n      - causal-reasoning\\n      - benchmark\\n      - machine-understanding\\n    pretty_name: FactoryBench\\n    size_categories:\\n      - 10K\u003cn\u003c100K\\n    configs:\\n      - config_name: level_1\\n        data_files:\\n          - split: train\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_1/train.jsonl\\n          - split: validation\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_1/validation.jsonl\\n          - split: test\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_1/test.jsonl\\n      - config_name: level_2\\n        data_files:\\n          - split: train\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_2/train.jsonl\\n          - split: validation\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_2/validation.jsonl\\n          - split: test\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_2/test.jsonl\\n      - config_name: level_3\\n        data_files:\\n          - split: train\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_3/train.jsonl\\n          - split: validation\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_3/validation.jsonl\\n          - split: test\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_3/test.jsonl\\n      - config_name: level_4\\n        data_files:\\n          - split: train\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_4/train.jsonl\\n          - split: validation\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_4/validation.jsonl\\n          - split: test\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_4/test.jsonl\\n    \\n\\n## Loading the data\\n    \\n    `from datasets import load_dataset\\n    \\n    # Load a single level/split\\n    ds = load_dataset(\\n        \\\"FactoryBench/FactoryBench\\\",\\n        data_files=\\\"factorybench_qa/level_1/test.jsonl\\\",\\n        split=\\\"train\\\",\\n    )\\n    \\n    # Load underlying telemetry\\n    import pandas as pd\\n    root = \\\"hf://datasets/FactoryBench/FactoryBench/factorywave\\\"\\n    episodes = pd.read_parquet(f\\\"{root}/episodes.parquet\\\")\\n    ur_125 = pd.read_parquet(f\\\"{root}/ur_signals.parquet\\\")\\n    ur_10  = pd.read_parquet(f\\\"{root}/ur_signals_10hz.parquet\\\")  # different episodes\\n    kuka   = pd.read_parquet(f\\\"{root}/kuka_signals.parquet\\\")\\n    screw  = pd.read_parquet(f\\\"{root}/ur_screwdriver_signals.parquet\\\")\\n    \\n    # Load the combined knowledge graph (machines, faults, error→protocol, ...)\\n    import json, urllib.request\\n    kg = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(\\n        \\\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/FactoryBench/FactoryBench/resolve/main/knowledge_graph/knowledge_graph.json\\\"\\n    ).read())\\n    `\\n\\n## Citation\\n\\n## Intended use \u0026 limitations\\n\\nIntended use. Benchmark evaluation of LLMs and time-series models on structured industrial Q\u0026A reasoning tasks (state, intervention, counterfactual, decision-making).\\n\\nLimitations. Domain-specific to factory and industrial robotic scenarios; may not generalise to open-domain Q\u0026A. Faults are atomic and drawn from a closed catalogue of 27 physically injected mechanisms — different from compound or gradual real-world faults. The dataset shows a size imbalance between Levels 2 and 3.\\n\\nOut-of-scope. Not intended for deployment in safety-critical, medical, legal, or financial decision systems without further validation by domain experts.\\n\\n## License\\n\\nReleased under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0) license. You may share and adapt the dataset for any purpose, including commercial, with appropriate attribution to the FactoryBench authors. The accompanying generator source code, evaluation scripts, LLM-as-judge prompts, and tooling (linked from the paper) are released separately under the MIT License.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nFactoryBench · Forgis Labs (https://www.forgis.com/papers/factorybench.html)\\nciteturn10search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; A benchmark for evaluating LLMs and time-series models on machine understanding over industrial robotic telemetry. ... FactoryWave is the dataset we collect alongside the benchmark to bridge the cobot-to-industrial-machine gap that public datasets miss. ...       title   = {FactoryBench: Evaluating Industrial Machine Understanding},\\n\\n## FactoryWave\\n\\nFactoryWave is the dataset we collect alongside the benchmark to bridge the cobot-to-industrial-machine gap that public datasets miss. It contributes 8,983 episodes recorded on a UR3 cobot at 125 Hz and a KUKA KR10 industrial arm at 83 Hz, covering three tasks (pick-and-place, screwing, peg-in-hole) and a catalogue of 27 systematically injected fault types spanning gripper failures, misconfigurations, collisions, and peg-in-hole-specific anomalies.\\n\\nUR3 cobot · KUKA KR10 · 8,983 episodes 3 tasks · 27 fault conditions\\n\\nImage: KUKA KR10 industrial arm experimental setup Image: UR3 executing peg-in-hole task Image: UR3 executing screwing task Image: UR3 cable collision fault Image: UR3 external arm disturbance fault Image: UR3 peg-in-hole task variation Image: UR3 additional axis weight fault Image: UR3 collision with cardboard box Image: UR3 screwing task variation Image: KUKA KR10 setup detail Image: UR3 hole obstruction fault for peg-in-hole Image: UR3 external arm disturbance during screwing Image: UR3 collision with rigid object Image: UR3 cable collision during peg-in-hole Image: UR3 unstable mounting platform fault Image: UR3 peg-in-hole task variation Image: UR3 screwing task variation Image: UR3 collision with foam cube Image: KUKA KR10 soft collision event Image: UR3 additional axis weight fault variation Image: UR3 external arm disturbance variation Image: UR3 peg-in-hole task variation Image: UR3 external arm disturbance during peg-in-hole Image: UR3 screwing task variation Image: UR3 collision with rigid object variation Image: UR3 external arm disturbance during screwing variation Image: UR3 unstable mounting platform variation Image: UR3 external arm disturbance during screwing variation\\n\\n## Getting started\\n\\nComing soon. Public dataset release and loader are in preparation. Check back here for the install command, the Hugging Face dataset, and a runnable evaluation script.\\n\\n## Citation\\n    \\n    `@article{factorybench2026,\\n      title   = {FactoryBench: Evaluating Industrial Machine Understanding},\\n      author  = {Merzouki, Yanis and Izquierdo, Coral and Ignuta-Ciuncanu, Matei and G{\\\\'o}mez-Bracamonte, Marcos and Maggioni, Riccardo and Lombardi, Alessandro and Mazzoleni, Camilla and Martelli, Federico and G{\\\\\\\"u}nther, Bal{\\\\'a}zs and Petersen, Jonas and Petersen, Philipp},\\n      journal = {arXiv preprint arXiv:2605.07675},\\n      year    = {2026}\\n    }`--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nFactoryNet: A Large-Scale Dataset toward Industrial Time-Series Foundation Models (https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.09081)\\nciteturn10academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Title: FactoryNet: A Large-Scale Dataset toward Industrial Time-Series Foundation Models\\nTitle: FactoryNet: A Large-Scale Dataset toward Industrial Time-Series Foundation Models\\nAuthors: Karim Othman, Jonas Petersen, Matei Ignuta-Ciuncanu, Camilla Mazzoleni, Federico Martelli, Alessandro Lombardi, Riccardo Maggioni, Philipp Petersen\\nDate: Sat May  9 17:45:36 2026\\n\\nWe introduce the first universal pretraining corpus for industrial time-series data: FactoryNet. 51M datapoints across 23k end-to-end task executions (13.3k real, 9.8k synthetic) on six embodiments, unified by a shared schema that enables robust zero-shot cross-embodiment transfer and highly parameter-efficient anomaly detection. We introduce a novel schema: Setpoint, Effort, Feedback, Context (S-E-F-C) underlying the whole pipeline that maps any actuated system into a common representational frame. The corpus spans 27 annotated anomaly types alongside healthy baselines and counterfactual pairs across robotic manipulation and machining domains. Cross-embodiment transfer experiments yield positive results: under bias-aware metrics our model demonstrates fair cross-embodiment transfer capabilities on the evaluated source-target pair, while 24 schema-aligned signals achieves competitive anomaly detection performance compared to high-dimensional baselines. We release FactoryNet as a growing, multi-embodiment dataset to drive progress toward industrial foundation models.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nFactoryBench (https://alex-wiki.langotime.ai/entities/factorybench-2026)\\nciteturn10search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last week;   * time-series ... FactoryBench is a 70,918-item Q\u0026A benchmark over industrial robotic multivariate telemetry. ...   * Official evaluation client: https://github.com/Forgis-Labs/FactoryBench ...   * Raw dataset metadata: source.md\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nfactorybench · PyPI (https://pypi.org/project/factorybench/0.0.15/)\\nciteturn10search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: last month; ###### GitHub Statistics ...   * Dataset ...   * Tags benchmark , evaluation , llm , language-models , time-series , industrial , robotics , causal-reasoning , factorybench\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nFactoryBench: Evaluating Industrial Machine Understanding (https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.07675)\\nciteturn10academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; We introduce FactoryBench, a benchmark for evaluating time-series models and LLMs on machine understanding over industrial robotic telemetry. ... We propose a scalable Q\u0026A generation framework built around structured question templates, present FactoryWave (a dense, multitask, multivariate sensor dataset collected from a UR3 cobot and a KUKA KR10 industrial arm), and construct FactoryBench as a large-scale benchmark of over 70k Q\u0026A items grounded in roughly 15k normalized episodes from FactoryWave, AURSAD, and voraus-AD.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nHarbor Hub (https://hub.harborframework.com/datasets/blobfishai/factorybench-100/latest)\\nciteturn10search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; FactoryBench-100 is a 100-task benchmark for employee-grade manufacturing and ERP decisions. ...   * Source and executable world: https://github.com/blobfishai/factory-agent-simulation\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nIndex of Production time series - Office for National Statistics (https://www.ons.gov.uk/economy/economicoutputandproductivity/output/datasets/indexofproduction)\\nciteturn10search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last week; # Dataset Index of Production time series ... Movements in the volume of production for the UK production industries: manufacturing, mining and quarrying, energy supply, and water and waste management.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nFactoryNet: A Large-Scale Dataset toward Industrial Time-Series Foundation Models (https://openreview.net/pdf/5a1bffc72e1fa4297b1946cd709e448d0062f516.pdf)\\nciteturn10search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; FactoryNet: A Large-Scale Dataset toward Industrial Time-Series Foundation Models ... For voraus-AD anomaly detection, we follow the official\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nFactorybench: Evaluating Industrial Machine Understanding: Code: Dataset | PDF | Causality | Time Series (https://www.scribd.com/document/1037817731/2605-07675v1)\\nciteturn10search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; Factorybench: Evaluating Industrial Machine Understanding: Code: DatasetFactoryBench is a benchmark designed to evaluate machine understanding in industrial robotics through time-series data and Q\u0026A tasks organized into four causal levels: state, intervention, counterfactual, and decision-making.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nManufacturing APIs (https://cdn.www.census.gov/topics/business-economy/manufacturing/data/api.html)\\nciteturn10search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.8 years ago; Crawled: 3 days ago; Census APIs Annual Survey of Manufactures (Time Series 2002-2016) December 16, 2016 Sample estimates of statistics for all manufacturing establishments with one or more paid employees.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nOECD Data Explorer • Production, sales, work started and orders (https://data-explorer.oecd.org/vis?df%5Bag%5D=OECD.SDD.STES\u0026df%5Bds%5D=dsDisseminateFinalDMZ\u0026df%5Bid%5D=DSD_STES%40DF_INDSERV\u0026df%5Bvs%5D=4.3\u0026dq=.M.PRVM......\u0026lc=en\u0026lo=5\u0026lom=LASTNPERIODS\u0026pg=0\u0026snb=232\u0026tm=industrial+production\u0026to%5BTIME_PERIOD%5D=false)\\nciteturn10search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; The Production and Sales dataset contains industrial statistics on four separate subjects: Production; Sales; Orders; and Work started. ... For Production, data comprise Indices of industrial production (IIP) for total industry, manufacturing, energy and crude petroleum; and further disaggregation of manufacturing production for intermediate goods and for investment goods and crude steel. ... Considerable effort has been made to ensure that the data are internationally comparable across all countries presented, coverage for as many countries as possible, and that all the subjects have reasonable length of time-series to assist analysis.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nData Files - Real-Time Data Set (IPT) (https://www.philadelphiafed.org/surveys-and-data/real-time-data-research/ipt)\\nciteturn10search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 weeks ago; Crawled: 5 days ago; Industrial Production Index: Total (IPT) ... The entire time-series history for each vintage (column) is available to the public at the vintage date shown in the column header.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nSmart Factories in the Era of Industry 4.0: Convergence of IoT and Cyber-Physical Systems for Intelligent Automation, Connectivity, and Resilient Manufacturing (https://www.atlantis-press.com/article/126019554.pdf)\\nciteturn10search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Our evaluation utilizes real-world manufacturing datasets totaling over 10 million data points collected from industrial ... The Sensor-Network-IoT dataset aggregates eight months of network-level data from multiple facilities with ... interpolation for time-series and predictive imputation for non-temporal data.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nAnalog and Multi-modal Manufacturing Datasets Acquired on the Future Factories Platform (https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.15544)\\nciteturn10academia16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.6 years ago; These datasets are generated by a manufacturing assembly line that utilizes industrial standards with respect to actuators, control mechanisms, and transducers. ... The datasets generated include a time series analog dataset and the other is a time series multi-modal dataset which includes images of the system alongside the analog data.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nTimeSeriesBench: An Industrial-Grade Benchmark for Time Series Anomaly Detection Models (https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.10802)\\nciteturn10academia17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.6 years ago; Title: TimeSeriesBench: An Industrial-Grade Benchmark for Time Series Anomaly Detection Models ... An industrial dataset is also released along with TimeSeriesBench.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nSemiconductor equipment and materials service, 1986-1990 (https://manuals.plus/m/2fab2f280c4aa3c80a9c7121c5cc2e003e146fa99e07b869ed7d73f89c6b122d.pdf)\\nciteturn10search18 [wordlim: 200] Published: 13.4 years ago; Factory Automation ... Aggiegata data for these categoiifiS are added to provide a consistent total for Sis woddwide wafer\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nfactoryNET\\n\\nDigital Transformation in Manufacturin (https://jasco.co.ke/media/brochures/factoryNET.pdf)\\nciteturn10search19 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 9 months ago; Digital Transformation in Manufacturing ... factoryNET is a set of digital tools that enable data collection, visualization, and control, data management, analytics, and reporting. ... DunayNET is a technology company specializing in the design and development of solutions for various industrial sectors based on IoT and ML/AI solutions as turnkey solutions.\\n\"","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa6418528e887d2be4b1f40d4eee535","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"summary":[{"text":"**Evaluating FactoryBench Integration**\n\nI'm considering the potential integration of FactoryBench in 2026, which seems relevant based on search results. It could really enhance business value, especially with the new dataset's Q\u0026A feature. However, there's a time constraint because I can't adapt OpenTSLM within three hours. I might want to use an ingestion pipeline to onboard the dataset and show evidence of data source integration. I'll need to be cautious with any unfinished tasks while assessing risks and maximizing scalability features without overpromising support.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"FactoryBench is actually relevant: it contains roughly 70k industrial time-series Q\u0026A items across UR and KUKA robots, with intervention and decision questions. It could broaden the roadmap from “one collision dataset” to “a reusable industrial investigation layer.” The safe hackathon move is to prove the ingestion boundary now, not pretend canary-v4 already generalizes to it.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa64188b29887d29fbc88c452f0f522","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_PXgYZbKk43TnQcgG3PPYebf9","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa64189ce0887d2b1136cfccc3bd0a1","input":"const r = await Promise.allSettled([\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg -n \\\"Bosch|Factory|onboard|ingest|source|preset|agent\\\" frontend/src data_ingestion -g '*.tsx' -g '*.ts' -g '*.py' | head -280\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":18000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg --files frontend/src/workspaces data_ingestion/src/dataset_profiler/onboarding | sort; sed -n '1,320p' frontend/src/workspaces/DataWorkspace.tsx 2\u003e/dev/null || true; sed -n '1,280p' frontend/src/workspaces/DatasetWorkspace.tsx 2\u003e/dev/null || true\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":26000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git show origin/codex/source-ingestion-integration:frontend/src/workspaces/DataWorkspace.tsx 2\u003e/dev/null | sed -n '1,340p'; git diff --stat origin/main...origin/codex/source-ingestion-integration\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":22000})\n]); for (const x of r) text(x.status===\"fulfilled\"?x.value.output:String(x.reason));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789280643.075718,"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_PXgYZbKk43TnQcgG3PPYebf9","id":"ctco_01a09970-0bb5-7911-ad71-72428edd0147","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789280652.213596,"turn_id":"01a0996f-3d85-7cb0-a76e-b2c8a2014ad0"},"outp