{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:32:11.524Z","ordinal":14585,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa64368e55487d2a2fa1e31d0578f53","status":"completed","call_id":"call_rUhyeEk5RJOwnE1kEl6MJW1t","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /tmp/trace-final-demo-impact-pr.md\\n+The demo previously showed the model result as text and required a second click to reveal its time cue. A completed OpenTSLM prediction now seeks directly to the generated onset, highlights the predicted joint, and labels the onset on the measured torque plot, so the core incident story is visible immediately while remaining distinct from publisher annotations.\\n+\\n+The data-source screen is also leaner: advanced controls are collapsed, and compact KUKA and FactoryBench presets demonstrate the existing sourcing pipeline's expansion path without claiming that canary-v4 already supports another robot domain.\\n+\\n+Validation:\\n+- `cd frontend && npm test` — 17 files, 94 tests passed\\n+- `cd frontend && npm run build` — passed\\n+- Live browser run against canary-v4 — predicted onset 6.063 s shown on the robot context and torque plot, with J4 highlighted\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a09973-2c14-7021-8bb8-3bdcb42353b2","create_time":1789281127.236033}}}
