{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:40:25.755Z","ordinal":15017,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09736-d5c6-7cc3-a099-0521c0b02bd2","turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa645520e1c87d299ec9ec6dcd2e628","summary_text":["**Evaluating training methods**\n\nOkay, the user wants a broad and calculated approach. I need to think about running the base OpenTSLM on FactoryBench mini through official benchmarks using textual prompts. However, that might not showcase the temporal numeric model effectively. \n\nIt could be better to fine-tune a generative LLM directly on FactoryBench contexts rather than OpenTSLM. There’s a lot to consider about using FactoryNet and the training risks involved, especially since FactoryBench has hundreds of episodes for more effective supervised multi-task learning. I need to ensure any integration is ready within time constraints."],"raw_content":[]},"started_at_ms":1789281618092,"completed_at_ms":1789281625755}}
