\",workdir:\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",yield_time_ms:30000,max_output_tokens:3000,sandbox_permissions:\"require_escalated\",justification:\"May I verify the final remote branch identities before reporting completion?\",\"prefix_rule\":[\"git\",\"ls-remote\"]})\n]);\nfor (const x of r) text(x.status === \"fulfilled\" ? x.value.output : String(x.reason));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281451.183259,"turn_id":"01a09973-2c14-7021-8bb8-3bdcb42353b2"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_sSd0Sr1IlW3BVZPoqWFgfJXA","id":"ctco_01a0997c-5647-7e11-b951-5e2c0e380e31","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281457.73517,"turn_id":"01a09973-2c14-7021-8bb8-3bdcb42353b2"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.1 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"✓ Metadata branches: OK (no remote-tracking metadata ref found)\n\n✓ Git hooks: OK\n✓ Codex hooks: INSTALLED\n  Codex-discovered hooks: /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/.codex/hooks.json\n✓ Codex hook approval records: PRESENT\n✓ Claude Code hook config: OK\n✓ OpenCode hook config: OK\n✓ Pi hook config: OK\nNo stuck sessions found.\n?? .cursor/\n?? .factory/\n?? .gemini/\n?? .github/\n?? .opencode/\n?? .pi/\nc09aa3e (HEAD -\u003e codex/final-demo-impact, origin/codex/final-demo-impact) Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into codex/final-demo-impact\n6316dd0 (origin/main, origin/HEAD) Merge pull request #19 from ukafkasyali/codex/source-ingestion-integration\ne9139ee Merge pull request #23 from ukafkasyali/codex/incident-cohorts\nba11891 feat(frontend): focus demo on predicted incident onset\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"mergeCommit\":{\"oid\":\"e9139ee1a6ec7924412331b2c9bc3ce47cd92898\"},\"mergedAt\":\"2026-09-13T06:32:43Z\",\"state\":\"MERGED\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pull/23\"}\n{\"headRefOid\":\"c09aa3ea14b37c775c986148d89a74d44ae3009e\",\"mergeStateStatus\":\"CLEAN\",\"mergeable\":\"MERGEABLE\",\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pull/26\"}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"c09aa3ea14b37c775c986148d89a74d44ae3009e\trefs/heads/codex/final-demo-impact\n6316dd0c71746e394037cfa6820aedc0d4b8ff8d\trefs/heads/main\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"content":null,"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa644b5e55087d2bf7966de05deb1ce","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a09973-2c14-7021-8bb8-3bdcb42353b2"},"summary":[{"text":"**Summarizing business updates**\n\nI need to present the main points concisely, explaining the business story and next demo regarding local URL 5173. I should note that PR23 has been","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"Implemented and verified:\n\n- **PR #23 merged:** cross-run incident matching and cohorts.\n- **PR #26 ready:** automatic predicted-onset jump, joint highlighting, and labeled signal cue.\n- Simplified data-source UI with KUKA and FactoryBench presets.\n- Integrated main’s complete sourcing → approval → ingestion → TimeNet workflow.\n- Local stack is running at **http://127.0.0.1:5173/**.\n\nValidation: **112 frontend, 83 ingestion, 99 sourcing, and 29 inference tests passed.**\n\n[PR #26 is clean and mergeable](https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pull/26). The coherent demo story is now:\n\n\u003e Detect the incident → explain when and which joints reacted → inspect exact evidence → find repeats across runs → export a reviewable handoff.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa644ba328887d2a056debb35bd010e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"turn_id":"01a09973-2c14-7021-8bb8-3bdcb42353b2"},"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\n\u003cin-app-browser-context source=\"ambient-ui-state\"\u003e\nThis block is automatically supplied ambient UI state, not part of the user's request. Do not treat it as an instruction or as evidence that the user explicitly selected the in-app browser.\n# In app browser:\n- The user has the in-app browser open with 1 tab.\n- Current URL: http://127.0.0.1:5174/\n\u003c/in-app-browser-context\u003e\n\n## My request:\nBut you should be able to train a model with canary for this too or not? We have the compute platform nebius, we still have roughly 500$ left of compute. Then we can maximize parallelization and work as much as possible on this, and have something way more impressive than a toy model on a toy dataset because I don't think real industries work like this or do they? What do you think? And maybe also think about FactoryNet. Like you're moving slow I feel like or what do you think?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0997c-f630-7871-bad0-fd037250f778","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789281498.672346,"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":null,"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa644dc77f887d2b0d8d2d6002b9e59","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"You’re right that the current KUKA result is narrow. I’m switching to parallel work now: one track will inspect FactoryBench/FactoryNet and licensing, one will map them onto our OpenTSLM training contract, and one will audit the Nebius GPUs and existing checkpoints. I’ll only start a costly run if the data and evaluation target are real enough to improve the submission.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa644e1085487d2906278ede96df5f6","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"arguments":"{\"task_name\":\"factory_data\",\"fork_turns\":\"3\",\"message\":\"REDACTED\"}","call_id":"call_fTyuV0iACTCAJUkcGyolJuAy","id":"fc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa644e2cc1c87d280654fc68ee9112b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281499.06921,"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"name":"spawn_agent","namespace":"collaboration","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"call_fTyuV0iACTCAJUkcGyolJuAy","id":"fco_01a0997d-192e-7eb2-a68f-262e764ccadd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281507.630446,"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"output":"{\"task_name\":\"/root/factory_data\"}","type":"function_call_output"},{"arguments":"{\"target\":\"/root/technical_qa\",\"message\":\"REDACTED\"}","call_id":"call_DjXRJYTXBGRuMQ6WanwIg1bg","id":"fc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa644e632b087d28cd7b65d2b000279","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281508.21173,"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"name":"followup_task","namespace":"collaboration","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"call_DjXRJYTXBGRuMQ6WanwIg1bg","id":"fco_01a0997d-27bf-76f1-8838-e8db6390fe2f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281511.359055,"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"output":"","type":"function_call_output"},{"arguments":"{\"target\":\"/root/judge_audit\",\"message\":\"REDACTED\"}","call_id":"call_zgkZW8Iza2W6noPLNjGoUJ72","id":"fc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa644eadf0487d2be25c1156fccabef","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281511.908927,"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"name":"followup_task","namespace":"collaboration","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"call_zgkZW8Iza2W6noPLNjGoUJ72","id":"fco_01a0997d-395e-7591-95c6-1a2c51bf586b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281515.870354,"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"output":"","type":"function_call_output"},{"content":null,"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa644ee02e487d28f29af7d42120161","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"arguments":"{\"target\":\"/root/product_critic\",\"message\":\"REDACTED\"}","call_id":"call_733iDuNilqXr4DY1xDuukLaC","id":"fc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa644ee48b087d295c3384a395e6766","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281516.307733,"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"name":"followup_task","namespace":"collaboration","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"call_733iDuNilqXr4DY1xDuukLaC","id":"fco_01a0997d-4877-7112-b6e1-12a44818c260","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281519.735097,"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"output":"collab tool failed: agent thread limit reached","type":"function_call_output"},{"content":null,"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa644f5b69087d295ff49aa4374fee1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_f8WW1aMroDJRX8etDZIBZroD","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa644f7d43487d2b71110069f6f9bad","input":"const r = await Promise.allSettled([\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git status --short \u0026\u0026 git branch --show-current \u0026\u0026 git log --oneline --decorate -4\",workdir:\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:4000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,260p' model_training/README.md; printf '\\\\n-- configs --\\\\n'; rg -n \\\"factory|canary|focused|8192|h100|nebius|ssh\\\" model_training inference docs -g '*.md' -g '*.yaml' -g '*.py' | head -240\",workdir:\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:18000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg --files model_training | sort | sed -n '1,260p'; printf '\\\\n-- sourcing/ingestion factory refs --\\\\n'; rg -n \\\"FactoryBench|FactoryNet|factorybench|factorynet\\\" . --glob '!frontend/node_modules/**' --glob '!.git/**'\",workdir:\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:18000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,260p' inference/README.md\",workdir:\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:16000})\n]);\nfor (const x of r) text(x.status === \"fulfilled\" ? x.value.output : String(x.reason));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281520.413396,"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_f8WW1aMroDJRX8etDZIBZroD","id":"ctco_01a0997d-7492-7c81-a8fa-b131da12bacd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281531.026402,"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"?? .cursor/\n?? .factory/\n?? .gemini/\n?? .github/\n?? .opencode/\n?? .pi/\ncodex/final-demo-impact\nc09aa3e (HEAD -\u003e codex/final-demo-impact, origin/codex/final-demo-impact) Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into codex/final-demo-impact\n6316dd0 (origin/main, origin/HEAD) Merge pull request #19 from ukafkasyali/codex/source-ingestion-integration\ne9139ee Merge pull request #23 from ukafkasyali/codex/incident-cohorts\nba11891 feat(frontend): focus demo on predicted incident onset\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"# Robot telemetry observability training\n\nThis package prepares raw KUKA LWR4+ external-joint-torque recordings and fine-tunes a generative\nOpenTSLM model to answer natural-language questions about contact, event semantics, affected joints,\nand event timing. It is the data/training half of the Foxglove-like observability demo.\n\nThe canonical path is **raw source -\u003e TimeNet connector -\u003e TimeF dataset -\u003e training-window\nadapter -\u003e model**. TimeF records preserve complete recordings, signal metadata, units, and event\nprovenance. The adapter validates that contract and materializes memory-mapped windows once so GPU\ntraining does not repeatedly decode Parquet. A new robot dataset should add a TimeNet connector and\nmapping rather than fork the training loop.\n\n## Audited submission comparison\n\nThe completed feature, OpenTSLM, Qwen plot and zero-signal predictions are archived in\n[`docs/submission/evaluation`](../docs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.md). Recompute the\nmatched 512-window comparison without heavy dependencies using:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 -m robot_observability.comparison \\\n  --source ../docs/submission/evaluation/source --output /tmp/trace-comparison\n```\n\nThe report validates example/target/split identity and distinguishes positive-contact F1 from\nanswer availability, complete-summary usability and recording-group uncertainty. The feature\nbaseline is stronger on classification; no OpenTSLM superiority is claimed.\n\n\n## Locked decisions\n\n- Full raw collision and intentional-contact corpora, not the leakage-prone quick-start CSVs.\n- 1.024 s, seven-channel external-torque windows at 1 kHz.\n- Manual `JK_moments.mat` marker as event-onset ground truth.\n- Event position jittered from 205–716 ms; recording folders are split before window generation.\n- 70/15/15 recording-grouped train/validation/test split, stratified by experiment class.\n- Train-only robust median/MAD scaling; signed torque and physical-unit statistics retained as\n  metadata but excluded from model prompts to prevent a textual shortcut.\n- Strongest-joint pseudo-label is calibrated top-5%-mean disturbance, not contact-location truth.\n- Natural-language evidence plus strict JSON output. Free motion uses `null` onset/joint fields.\n- Primary TSLM: OpenTSLM SoftPrompt + Llama 3.2 1B + HAR warm start.\n- Training checkpoints contain only tensors and primitive flags, so inference can\n  validate them with PyTorch's weights-only loader before release.\n- Baselines: transparent signal features and Qwen3-VL 4B over equivalent seven-panel plots.\n- Retrospective observability only; this is not a causal collision detector or safety controller.\n\nSee [the design decisions](docs/design.md), [dataset documentation](docs/dataset.md), and\n[remote runbook](docs/runbook.md).\n\n## Local commands\n\n```bash\nuv venv\nuv pip install -e '.[train,dev,timenet]'\n\nrobot-observe download --output data/raw\nPYTHONPATH=../data_ingestion/src python ../data_ingestion/scripts/build_kuka_timef_dataset.py \\\n  data/raw/collision artifacts/timef-raw --part part1\nPYTHONPATH=../data_ingestion/src python ../data_ingestion/scripts/build_kuka_timef_dataset.py \\\n  data/raw/contact artifacts/timef-raw --part part2\n\nrobot-observe prepare-timef --config configs/data_timef.yaml \\\n  --timef-version artifacts/timef-raw/kuka/collision-part1/1.0.0 \\\n  --timef-version artifacts/timef-raw/kuka/contact-part2/1.0.0\nrobot-observe baseline --prepared-root data/prepared/timef-v1 \\\n  --output-root artifacts/baseline/signal-features-512 --limit 512\n\npython -m robot_observability.train_opentslm \\\n  --prepared-root data/prepared/timef-v1 \\\n  --run-name llama-har-sp-smoke \\\n  --smoke --max-steps 200\n```\n\nEvery expensive operation is resumable or refuses to overwrite prior artifacts. Training emits an\natomic `status.json`, append-only `metrics.jsonl`, TensorBoard events, generated validation samples,\nW\u0026B prediction tables with seven-channel signal previews, real-versus-zero-signal canaries, and\n`best_model.pt`/`last_model.pt` adapters. Every run also keeps a fixed, class-balanced probe from the\nactual training subset. Its teacher-forced loss, decoded task metrics, exact-answer fit, matched-prompt\nvalidation gap, and zero-signal response are tracked separately so a rapid token-loss drop cannot be\nmistaken for task learning.\n\nRun the capacity/fit check before another expensive run:\n\n```bash\npython -m robot_observability.train_opentslm \\\n  --prepared-root data/prepared/timef-v1 \\\n  --run-name llama-har-sp-fit-probe \\\n  --smoke --max-steps 320\npython scripts/report_fit_probe.py --run-dir runs/llama-har-sp-fit-probe\n```\n\nUse `--strict` on the reporter only when it should block the next launch. Its thresholds are diagnostic\ndefaults, not benchmark acceptance criteria.\n\n-- configs --\ndocs/submission/CHECKPOINT_HANDOFF.md:19:| Artifact role | Promoted OpenTSLM SoftPrompt checkpoint (canary-v4) | Private on Nebius; destination not approved here |\ndocs/submission/CHECKPOINT_HANDOFF.md:27:| Training configuration | [`opentslm_sp.yaml`](../../model_training/configs/opentslm_sp.yaml) is the current candidate default, not proven to be the canary-v4 run-resolved file | **Missing: recover the exact canary-v4 run configuration and its SHA-256; it was not present in the deployed VM bundle** |\ndocs/submission/CHECKPOINT_HANDOFF.md:28:| Deployed runtime configuration | `kuka-sp-canary-v4.config.json`; file SHA-256 `3566c2f01b343b4658653b24126b2ec377848dcfcacc82bdd568d7fd63505c19`; canonical JSON configuration digest starts `4dbdd82f5ff7` in the live receipt | Verified read-only on the VM 13 Sep 2026; transfer this exact file with the checkpoint |\ndocs/submission/CHECKPOINT_HANDOFF.md:30:| Normalization | training-only robust normalization for canary-v4; deployed file SHA-256 `f29e5dea6846d14ef7dc4da6ee55addca264b33439d0de4f8c57201a578f334b`, byte-identical to [`normalization.json`](evaluation/source/normalization.json) | Resolved; transfer the archived file and do not use query statistics |\ndocs/submission/CHECKPOINT_HANDOFF.md:32:| Archived canary-v4 output contract | `answer_then_evidence`: `Answer: {JSON}` followed by `Evidence:` | Verified from archived canary-v4 predictions; attach the exact prompt/template revision and schema |\ndocs/submission/CHECKPOINT_HANDOFF.md:33:| Current candidate training config | `rationale_then_answer`, deterministic signal pseudolabel source | Candidate configuration only; do not represent it as the released canary-v4 contract without matching artifact evidence |\ndocs/submission/CHECKPOINT_HANDOFF.md:67:5. Preserve the current private canary-v4 service unchanged. A handoff is not a\ndocs/submission/UI_WALKTHROUGH.md:1:# Three real examples through canary-v4\ndocs/submission/UI_WALKTHROUGH.md:13:3. Under **Event investigation**, check the selected interval and **canary-v4**, then\ndocs/submission/UI_WALKTHROUGH.md:30:| Example | Recording / split | Raw interval (seconds) | Observed canary-v4 output | Receipt |\ndocs/submission/UI_WALKTHROUGH.md:68:fitting. Real model answers still pass through the existing private canary-v4 service.\ndocs/submission/UI_WALKTHROUGH.md:146:5.641 s; selecting marker 27 at 165.529 s placed replay at 165.129 s. CPU canary-v4\ndocs/submission/UI_WALKTHROUGH.md:156:samples and the unchanged canary-v4 checkpoint/config. It predicted accidental\ndocs/submission/VERIFICATION.md:11:| Training focused suite | 54 passed; the TimeNet connector and training-observability modules additionally require TimeNet and TensorBoard in this environment |\ndocs/submission/VERIFICATION.md:19:| Private deployed model | Ready; expected canary-v4 SHA-256; real `inference.smoke` passed |\ndocs/submission/VERIFICATION.md:25:The complete optional training suite cannot collect the TimeNet connector test without TimeNet or the training-observability test without TensorBoard in this environment. The 54-test focused suite includes the remaining training tests; it is not a claim that GPU training was rerun. The live smoke confirms actual inference with the existing deployed checkpoint.\ndocs/submission/PRODUCT_PRIORITIES.md:17:   by the canary smoke test. Keep GPU training independent of this integration.\ndocs/submission/PRODUCT_PRIORITIES.md:56:for canary-v4. Split by independent tool, bearing or engine histories; evaluate\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/train_opentslm.py:59:        raise ValueError(\"Stratified generation canary requires summary mode\")\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/train_opentslm.py:979:        \"generation_canary_class_counts\": dict(\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/train_opentslm.py:985:        \"generation_canary_joint_counts\": dict(\ndocs/submission/README.md:19:| Working evidence-linked demo | [Demo script](DEMO.md), [smoke receipt](demo/smoke-result.json), [readable handoff](demo/investigation-example.md), [audit JSON](demo/investigation-example.json) | Private canary-v4 path was smoke-tested; exports retain telemetry receipt, measurements and prediction separately | The three fixed examples are not a quality benchmark; raw coverage remains limited |\ndocs/submission/README.md:20:| Checkpoint or adapter handoff | [Release procedure](../../inference/README.md), [handoff checklist](CHECKPOINT_HANDOFF.md) | Service reports canary-v4 checkpoint digest `8ff63b84ae5b64758f66b3e0527f4f225a04bb2b6b39193c806f58d94cec9f23`; the local backbone weight file matches the official immutable Hub blob by SHA-256 | Approved submission-channel delivery is still required; the live receipt still prints `backbone:unknown` for the local path |\ndocs/submission/DEMO.md:9:Timing, measured 13 September 2026 on the current CPU-only deployment (two smoke runs through the SSH tunnel): one full analyze-interval round trip takes about **24 seconds**. Do not start another query during the timed demo. Say that the visible result is the current canary-v4 output for this exact 7×1,024 input. If a judge requests fresh inference, run it after the core story. Only one query is served at a time; do not queue clicks.\ninference/README.md:34:ssh -t samet@89.169.110.3 '~/trace-inference/inference/.venv/bin/hf auth login'\ninference/README.md:42:tmux respawn-pane -k -t trace-inference -c /home/samet/trace-inference 'exec env TRACE_MODEL_CONFIG=inference/kuka-sp-canary-v4.config.json TRACE_DEVICE=cpu OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 MKL_NUM_THREADS=4 inference/.venv/bin/python -m inference.server \u003e\u003e inference/server.log 2\u003e\u00261'\ninference/README.md:95:ssh YOUR_USER@YOUR_VM_IP\ninference/README.md:114:ssh YOUR_USER@YOUR_VM_IP 'mkdir -p ~/trace-inference/inference ~/trace-inference/frontend/public/data'\ninference/README.md:170:ssh -N -L 127.0.0.1:8000:127.0.0.1:8000 YOUR_USER@YOUR_VM_IP\ninference/README.md:288:Official references: [Nebius VM quickstart](https://docs.nebius.com/compute/quickstart),\ninference/README.md:289:[Nebius SSH connection](https://docs.nebius.com/compute/virtual-machines/connect),\ninference/README.md:329:private deployment retains canary-v4's exact promoted checkpoint and training\ninference/README.md:336:The live canary-v4 checkpoint/config is unchanged, but inference temporarily runs\ndocs/PARALLEL_AGENT_BRIEFS.md:37:The deployed model is canary-v4, immutable at process startup, SHA-256\ndocs/PARALLEL_AGENT_BRIEFS.md:62:run focused checks, inspect the diff, commit only your intended files, and open a\ndocs/PARALLEL_AGENT_BRIEFS.md:63:focused draft PR against current main. Do not merge or deploy it from the worker\ndocs/PARALLEL_AGENT_BRIEFS.md:117:Use local fixtures and clean environment validation where possible. Deliver focused\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/comparison.py:32:    \"opentslm\": \"OpenTSLM canary-v4 (trained Llama 3.2 1B)\",\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/augmentation.py:1:\"\"\"Leakage-safe, task-focused training curriculum for robot telemetry.\"\"\"\nmodel_training/configs/opentslm_sp.yaml:15:  max_examples: 8192\nmodel_training/configs/opentslm_sp_focused_control.yaml:18:  max_examples: 8192\nmodel_training/configs/opentslm_sp_joint_permutation.yaml:18:  max_examples: 8192\nmodel_training/docs/baseline_comparison.md:13:- **OpenTSLM canary:** semantics macro-F1 `0.8845`, contact F1 `0.9871`, median onset error\nmodel_training/docs/baseline_comparison.md:20:baseline. Against the OpenTSLM canary, the CNN wins event semantics, median onset error, and output\nmodel_training/docs/baseline_comparison.md:35:The OpenTSLM row is not yet a fair full-budget comparison. It is explicitly a canary result from a\nmodel_training/docs/runbook.md:8:ssh nebius-h100\nmodel_training/docs/runbook.md:30:ssh -L 6006:127.0.0.1:6006 nebius-h100\nmodel_training/scripts/monitor_training.py:102:            \"The zero-signal canary is paired but smaller than the 48-window generation canary.\",\nmodel_training/scripts/monitor_training.py:234:        alerts.append(\"RED: zero-signal canary does not cover all three event classes\")\nmodel_training/tests/test_augmentation.py:38:def test_curriculum_has_three_focused_views_and_remaps_joint_target() -\u003e None:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"model_training/README.md\nmodel_training/challenge_description.md\nmodel_training/configs/cnn_1d.yaml\nmodel_training/configs/data.yaml\nmodel_training/configs/data_timef.yaml\nmodel_training/configs/opentslm_sp.yaml\nmodel_training/configs/opentslm_sp_focused_control.yaml\nmodel_training/configs/opentslm_sp_joint_permutation.yaml\nmodel_training/configs/opentslm_sp_qwen_fallback.yaml\nmodel_training/configs/qwen3_vl.yaml\nmodel_training/docs/assets/qwen3-vl-input-accidental-contact.png\nmodel_training/docs/baseline-methods-explained.tsx\nmodel_training/docs/baseline_comparison.md\nmodel_training/docs/dataset.md\nmodel_training/docs/design.md\nmodel_training/docs/opentslm_research.md\nmodel_training/docs/runbook.md\nmodel_training/pyproject.toml\nmodel_training/scripts/audit_prepared_equivalence.py\nmodel_training/scripts/build_timef.py\nmodel_training/scripts/compare_models.py\nmodel_training/scripts/diagnose_opentslm_generation.py\nmodel_training/scripts/download_zenodo.py\nmodel_training/scripts/eval_plot_vlm.py\nmodel_training/scripts/evaluate_grounding_panel.py\nmodel_training/scripts/evaluate_opentslm.py\nmodel_training/scripts/monitor_training.py\nmodel_training/scripts/post_training.py\nmodel_training/scripts/report_fit_probe.py\nmodel_training/scripts/run_one_shot_when_gpu_free.sh\nmodel_training/scripts/run_overnight_joint_permutation.sh\nmodel_training/scripts/run_qwen_plot_benchmark.sh\nmodel_training/scripts/sanity_check_equivariance.py\nmodel_training/scripts/smoke_model_load.py\nmodel_training/scripts/train_cnn.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/__init__.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/augmentation.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/baseline.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/checkpoints.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/cli.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/cnn_baseline.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/comparison.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/config.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/constants.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/data/__init__.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/data/prepare.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/data/pseudolabels.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/data/raw.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/data/splits.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/data/timef.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/data/zenodo.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/metrics.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/opentslm_dataset.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/plot_baseline.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/prepared.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/qa.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/timenet_connector/__init__.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/timenet_connector/connector.py\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/timenet_connector/dataset.yaml\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/train_opentslm.py\nmodel_training/tests/test_augmentation.py\nmodel_training/tests/test_baseline.py\nmodel_training/tests/test_checkpoints.py\nmodel_training/tests/test_cnn_baseline.py\nmodel_training/tests/test_comparison.py\nmodel_training/tests/test_fit_probe_report.py\nmodel_training/tests/test_metrics.py\nmodel_training/tests/test_plot_baseline.py\nmodel_training/tests/test_pseudolabels.py\nmodel_training/tests/test_qa.py\nmodel_training/tests/test_raw.py\nmodel_training/tests/test_splits.py\nmodel_training/tests/test_timef_adapter.py\nmodel_training/tests/test_timenet_connector.py\nmodel_training/tests/test_training_observability.py\n\n-- sourcing/ingestion factory refs --\n./frontend/src/sourcing/DatasetScout.tsx:8:const factoryBrief = 'Find the FactoryBench industrial robot telemetry and question-answer dataset from https://huggingface.co/datasets/FactoryBench/FactoryBench for cross-robot fault reasoning research';\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"# Trace → OpenTSLM on Nebius\n\nStatus (13 September 2026): deployed privately on the team's Nebius H100 VM in\n`/home/samet/trace-inference`, using Python 3.12 and an isolated virtual environment.\nThe KUKA OpenTSLM-SP adapter is loaded and the SSH tunnel, Vite proxy and real\n1,024-sample inference path pass. The service reports the exact checkpoint digest;\nit never silently switches to a newer training artifact. The current process uses\nCPU because a teammate's training run owns the GPU; do not restart it on CUDA until\nthe training owner confirms that GPU memory is available.\n\nA training endpoint does not serve predictions automatically: this separate process\nloads an exported checkpoint once, then handles on-demand requests from Trace.\n\n### CNN comparison endpoint\n\nThe server can also expose the trained 1D CNN when `TRACE_CNN_CONFIG` points to a\nJSON config based on `cnn.config.example.json`. The config must name the CNN\ncheckpoint and the exact train-split `normalization.json` used for training. The\nCNN accepts all seven canonical channels and exactly 1,024 synchronized samples;\nother windows are rejected rather than resampled. Once loaded, `GET /api/models`\nadvertises `cnn-1d`, and Trace's comparison workspace runs it alongside OpenTSLM.\n\n```bash\nexport TRACE_CNN_CONFIG=/home/samet/trace-inference/inference/cnn.config.json\nTRACE_DEVICE=cuda python -m inference.server\n```\n\n### Resume this deployment\n\nThe VM is `samet@89.169.110.3`. After your Hugging Face account has access to the\nbase model, authenticate privately (do not paste tokens into chat or source code):\n\n```bash\nssh -t samet@89.169.110.3 '~/trace-inference/inference/.venv/bin/hf auth login'\n```\n\nThe process is in the `trace-inference` tmux session. After authentication, restart\nthat process only; the inference service does not automatically reload failed\nweights. From inside the VM:\n\n```bash\ntmux respawn-pane -k -t trace-inference -c /home/samet/trace-inference 'exec env TRACE_MODEL_CONFIG=inference/kuka-sp-canary-v4.config.json TRACE_DEVICE=cpu OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 MKL_NUM_THREADS=4 inference/.venv/bin/python -m inference.server \u003e\u003e inference/server.log 2\u003e\u00261'\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health\n```\n\nWait for `ready: true` before running the smoke test. The local frontend now uses\n`VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api` in gitignored `.env.local`; reconnect the SSH tunnel below\nif the local session ends. This VM has no passwordless sudo; its environment was\ncreated with the official user-local `uv` installer without changing system Python:\n\n```bash\n~/.local/bin/uv venv --python /usr/bin/python3 ~/trace-inference/inference/.venv\n~/.local/bin/uv pip install --python ~/trace-inference/inference/.venv/bin/python -r ~/trace-inference/inference/requirements.txt\n```\n\nDo not recreate the existing environment just to restart the service.\n\n## 1. Find the machine and checkpoint\n\nIn the Nebius console, choose your team's project, then **Compute → Virtual\nmachines**. Open a running VM and inspect its GPU type/count, public IP and SSH\nconnection instructions. If the list is empty, check other projects/regions.\nAn allocated training job is not necessarily a persistent VM you can SSH into.\n\nAsk Atakan for:\n\n\u003e Which architecture are you training (OpenTSLM-SP or Flamingo), which base LLM,\n\u003e and where is the exported checkpoint? Please share the training config, including\n\u003e normalization, channel order, sampling/window length, prompt template and LoRA\n\u003e settings. Is there a GPU VM we can use for inference without competing with training?\n\nThe first runtime supports **OpenTSLM-SP** with strict encoder/projector loading\nand explicit LoRA settings. The initial config uses the official\n`OpenTSLM/llama-3.2-1b-tsqa-sp` checkpoint. It was trained on TSQA, **not KUKA**;\nseven robot channels and this prompt are out-of-domain. A plausible answer is\nnot a model-quality result. Keep local numerical calculations as the factual check.\n\nFor Flamingo or a modified training fork, share the config first: upstream uses a\ndifferent state format and permissive checkpoint loading. This service deliberately\nfails on an unsupported architecture instead of silently serving partial weights.\n\n## 2. Prepare one GPU VM\n\nIf no suitable VM exists, create a plain GPU VM in Nebius with an Ubuntu CUDA\nimage and your **public** SSH key. One GPU is the starting point; check the available\nGPU's price, memory and quota before creation. A GPU cluster/Kubernetes is unnecessary\nfor this single-process smoke test. Use persistent storage for model caches and\ncheckpoints, and enough free disk for PyTorch/CUDA dependencies and weights (100 GiB\nis a practical starting allocation, not a measured minimum).\n\nPrefer a separate GPU or run after training pauses; two processes can exhaust VRAM.\nFrom your Mac, test the connection using the username from the VM configuration:\n\n```bash\nssh YOUR_USER@YOUR_VM_IP\nnvidia-smi\npython3 --version\n```\n\nThese commands assume Python 3.12 on the VM. The supplied requirements pin the\nupstream source and core ML dependencies; actual CUDA execution still needs its\nfirst GPU smoke test. If necessary on Ubuntu:\n\n```bash\nsudo apt-get update\nsudo apt-get install -y python3-venv git tmux\n```\n\n## 3. Copy this isolated service\n\nFrom the repository root on your Mac (this also works before committing):\n\n```bash\nssh YOUR_USER@YOUR_VM_IP 'mkdir -p ~/trace-inference/inference ~/trace-inference/frontend/public/data'\nscp inference/*.py inference/requirements.txt inference/smoke.config.json YOUR_USER@YOUR_VM_IP:~/trace-inference/inference/\nscp frontend/public/data/kuka-demo.json YOUR_USER@YOUR_VM_IP:~/trace-inference/frontend/public/data/\n```\n\nOn the VM:\n\n```bash\ncd ~/trace-inference\npython3 -m venv inference/.venv\nsource inference/.venv/bin/activate\npython -m pip install --upgrade pip\npython -m pip install -r inference/requirements.txt\npython -m pip check\npython -m pip freeze \u003e inference/requirements.resolved.txt\npython -c 'import torch; print(torch.__version__); print(torch.cuda.is_available())'\nhf auth login\n```\n\nThe Llama backbone may require your Hugging Face account to have accepted its\nlicense/access terms. Authenticate on the VM interactively; never put its token in\nthe frontend, a URL, a screenshot or a committed config. Use only checkpoints from\nthe official publisher or your team's trusted training process.\n\nStart a persistent terminal session, then the server:\n\n```bash\ntmux new -s trace-inference\ncd ~/trace-inference\nsource inference/.venv/bin/activate\nTRACE_DEVICE=cuda python -m inference.server 2\u003e\u00261 | tee inference/server.log\n```\n\nTo expose every authorized source recording through the same replay contract, mount\nthe trusted extracted KUKA archive and pass its root explicitly:\n\n```bash\nTRACE_DEVICE=cuda python -m inference.server --raw-root /absolute/path/to/kuka/raw\n```\n\nThe root must contain `\u003carchive\u003e/\u003crecording-id\u003e/JK_MsrExtTrq.mat` and the matching\n`JK_moments.mat`. At startup the adapter validates the original 1 kHz time axis,\nseven-channel shape, finite values, publisher marker bounds and file hashes. The\nfrontend receives a 100 Hz overview, then requests an exact 1,024-sample raw window\nonly for the selected analysis interval. It never resamples raw model input.\n\nDetach with Ctrl+B, then D. The server binds to **127.0.0.1:8000** by default. Keep\nit private; this development bridge is not an authenticated public API. It exposes\nreadiness at `/api/health` and actual availability at `/api/models` while weights\nload. No successful placeholder response is substituted on failure.\n\n## 4. Connect Trace and run the real smoke test\n\nOn your Mac, keep this tunnel running:\n\n```bash\nssh -N -L 127.0.0.1:8000:127.0.0.1:8000 YOUR_USER@YOUR_VM_IP\n```\n\nFrom the repository root, in another terminal:\n\n```bash\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health\npython3 -m inference.smoke\n```\n\nThe smoke command fails unless it gets a completed answer, checkpoint identity,\nthe exact selected evidence window and a receipt for **1,024 samples per channel**.\nIt saves `inference/smoke-result.json` (gitignored). Server logs also record an input\nhash. This checks the application path and interval handling; it is not an independent\nGPU attestation or an accuracy benchmark.\n\nThen restart Vite with connected services enabled:\n\n```bash\ncd frontend\nVITE_API_BASE_URL=/api npm run dev -- --port 5174\n```\n\nThe existing `/api` development proxy targets the local SSH tunnel. Alternatively\nset `VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api` in `frontend/.env.local`, then restart Vite. For a\ndeployed frontend, configure a same-origin reverse proxy; Vite's dev proxy is not\nincluded in a production build.\n\nOpen Trace and keep the initial interval **[5.787, 6.811) seconds**. The header must\nshow **OpenTSLM connected**. Click **Analyze interval** and wait for the structured\nprediction, measurements, input receipt and handoff actions. Only OpenTSLM is exposed\nby this service; there is no live CNN selector or endpoint. The measurements-only\nmode remains available under **Ask a custom question**.\n\nWith `--raw-root`, the backend catalog also lists the validated full recordings.\nOpen one, choose any publisher marker, and run the resulting 1.024-second interval.\nThe UI loads that exact raw interval on demand and preserves its input receipt in\nthe exported investigation. Publisher markers remain annotations and are never sent\nto the model.\n\n## 5. Switch to the team's checkpoint\n\nCopy `smoke.config.json` to a gitignored `inference/team.local.json`. Set:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"architecture\": \"sp\",\n  \"model_id\": \"team-kuka-sp\",\n  \"base_model\": \"meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B\",\n  \"checkpoint_path\": \"/absolute/persistent/path/to/exported-checkpoint.pt\",\n  \"normalization\": \"zscore_sample\",\n  \"max_new_tokens\": 128\n}\n```\n\nThis example is **not** a guess at your team's training configuration. Confirm every\nfield and align `prepare_sample()` with its prompt and preprocessing before using\nthe trained model. Supported normalization options are `zscore_sample` (per channel,\nsample standard deviation; same numerical convention as upstream TSQA) and `none`.\nIf training used LoRA, add `lora` with the exact `lora_r`, `lora_alpha`,\n`lora_dropout` and `target_modules` passed to upstream `enable_lora()`.\n\n```bash\nTRACE_MODEL_CONFIG=inference/team.local.json TRACE_DEVICE=cuda python -m inference.server\n```\n\nStop the previous server before starting the replacement. Re-run the smoke test,\nthen evaluate held-out recordings against the CNN and numerical baseline.\n\n### Promote an evaluated training run\n\nNew training runs now write tensor-only `best_model.pt` and `last_model.pt` files\nthat the inference runtime can load with `weights_only=True`. After\n`post_training.py` reaches `state: complete`, stage the exact artifact and generate\nthe next service config:\n\n```bash\npython -m inference.release \\\n  --candidate /path/to/run/best_model.pt \\\n  --post-training-status /path/to/run/post_training_status.json \\\n  --active-config inference/kuka-sp-v2.config.json \\\n  --models-dir models \\\n  --output-config inference/kuka-sp-next.config.json\n```\n\nThe command refuses incomplete evaluations, unsafe checkpoint payloads and LoRA\nconfiguration mismatches. It stores an immutable digest-named checkpoint and a\nrelease manifest. Review the held-out metrics, point the tmux startup command at\nthe generated config, restart once, and run `python -m inference.smoke`. Keep the\nprevious config until the smoke test passes so rollback is one restart.\n\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"content":null,"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa644fe54b887d2a12722c1a636f52e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_lzwzARfRnCjRe7rj2Kb5eKD4","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa644ff08f887d2b3e92054af3a1d85","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,180p' model_training/docs/runbook.md; sed -n '1,220p' model_training/scripts/run_one_shot_when_gpu_free.sh; sed -n '1,220p' model_training/configs/opentslm_sp_focused_control.yaml\",workdir:\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:16000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281531.634229,"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_lzwzARfRnCjRe7rj2Kb5eKD4","id":"ctco_01a0997d-881e-7072-a8ff-e120751fca2a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281536.030382,"turn_id":"01a0997c-f501-7f93-983c-d050681a889a"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"# Nebius H100 runbook\n\nRemote workspace: `/home/atakantopaloglu/ysamet-training`.\n\n## Persistent jobs\n\n```bash\nssh nebius-h100\ntmux list-sessions\ntail -f /home/atakantopaloglu/ysamet-training/download.log\n```\n\nThe data downloader also writes `data/raw/download_state.jsonl`. It resumes partial curl transfers,\nvalidates Zenodo checksums, and marks each extracted archive.\n\n## Authentication\n\n```bash\n/home/atakantopaloglu/ysamet-training/.auth-venv/bin/hf auth whoami\n```\n\nNever put the token in this repository or a command log.\n\n## Observing a training run\n\n```bash\ntail -f runs/\u003crun\u003e/stdout.log\ntail -f runs/\u003crun\u003e/metrics.jsonl\nwatch -n 2 nvidia-smi\nssh -L 6006:127.0.0.1:6006 nebius-h100\n```\n\nOn the remote host, serve TensorBoard with:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/tensorboard --logdir runs --host 127.0.0.1 --port 6006\n```\n\nThen open `http://127.0.0.1:6006` locally. `status.json` is safe for the demo backend to poll while\nthe append-only JSONL retains full history.\n\nThe main W\u0026B run exposes these complementary views:\n\n- `data/training_manifest`: all selected training examples with stable source index, record/session ID,\n  prompt variant, complete supervised answer, and target. The local JSONL and prepared arrays are SHA-256\n  pinned in `run_manifest.json`.\n- `data/training_probe_examples`: 48 event×intent-balanced examples from that exact selection, including\n  a seven-channel normalized-signal preview with target onset/evidence markers.\n- `training_probe/*`: teacher-forced loss and decoded metrics on those same examples, including strict\n  schema and answer fit.\n- `validation_matched/loss`: a validation loss using the same deterministic mixed-prompt distribution\n  as training. Use this—not the all-intents model-selection loss—for a generalization-gap comparison.\n- `training_probe_zero_signal/*`: paired predictions after removing the numeric signal.\n- `optimization/*`: pre-clip gradient norm, pre-step parameter norm, post-step learning rate, actual\n  update norm/parameter ratio, and gradient coverage for the encoder, projector, and LoRA groups.\n- `training_probe/predictions` and `validation/samples`: versioned prediction tables with signal plots.\n\nBefore a full launch, run a 32-example capacity probe and inspect/report it:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m robot_observability.train_opentslm \\\n  --prepared-root data/prepared/v1 \\\n  --run-name llama-har-sp-fit-probe \\\n  --smoke --max-steps 320\n.venv/bin/python scripts/report_fit_probe.py \\\n  --run-dir runs/llama-har-sp-fit-probe\n```\n\nThe report refuses to pass an unfinished run and checks decoded per-intent answers plus meaningful\npaired signal ablation in addition to token loss.\nAdd `--strict` only if a nonzero exit should gate the next run.\n\nAfter training, evaluate a fixed held-out subset without using it for model selection:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python scripts/evaluate_opentslm.py \\\n  --checkpoint runs/\u003crun\u003e/best_model.pt \\\n  --output artifacts/evaluation/\u003crun\u003e-test\n```\n\nFor an unattended run, `scripts/post_training.py` waits for the training tmux session to exit, then\nruns the same held-out evaluation plus temporal-shift and channel-permutation grounding checks. It\nwrites an atomic `post_training_status.json` and can resume the W\u0026B run to attach final metrics.\n\n## Plot baseline environment\n\nThis baseline does no fitting. It sends leak-free seven-channel plots to a frozen Qwen3-VL model and\nscores the same summary JSON contract as OpenTSLM. Do not start its server while an OpenTSLM process\nis using the H100.\n\nKeep vLLM separate so its Torch/CUDA dependency resolution cannot alter the training environment:\n\n```bash\nuv venv .vlm-venv\nuv pip install --python .vlm-venv/bin/python 'vllm\u003e=0.11,\u003c1' qwen-vl-utils==0.0.14 \\\n  -e '.[plot-baseline]'\n.vlm-venv/bin/vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct \\\n  --revision ebb281ec70b05090aa6165b016eac8ec08e71b17 \\\n  --port 8000 --dtype bfloat16 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.70\n```\n\nUse BF16 for the primary plot baseline: this cached 4B checkpoint is about 8.3 GB and comfortably\nfits an otherwise idle H100, while quantization could needlessly weaken the comparator. A vetted\npre-quantized AWQ checkpoint can be run as a separate secondary baseline:\n\n```bash\n.vlm-venv/bin/vllm serve \u003cverified-awq-model-id\u003e \\\n  --revision \u003cexact-hugging-face-commit\u003e \\\n  --port 8000 --dtype bfloat16 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.70\n.vlm-venv/bin/python scripts/eval_plot_vlm.py \\\n  --model \u003cverified-awq-model-id\u003e --model-revision \u003cexact-hugging-face-commit\u003e \\\n  --quantization awq --output artifacts/evaluation/qwen3-vl-awq-plot-test\n```\n\nDo not label an unverified community checkpoint as the primary Qwen result. The installed vLLM 0.29\nserver has no BitsAndBytes load-format entry, so the older\n`--quantization bitsandbytes --load-format bitsandbytes` recipe is not used here. Set `quantization`\nto the server's actual mode before evaluation. The\nevaluator checks the served model, captures the vLLM version, and writes an immutable manifest with\nthe prepared-record hash, exact record IDs, prompt hash, plot settings, and decoding settings. The\nselection algorithm and seed intentionally match `scripts/evaluate_opentslm.py`, so the two models\nare scored on identical windows and the natural held-out class distribution.\n\nRun a 12-record plumbing check first, then use a new directory for the locked 512-record benchmark:\n\n```bash\n.vlm-venv/bin/python scripts/eval_plot_vlm.py \\\n  --output artifacts/evaluation/qwen3-vl-plot-smoke --limit 12 --wandb-mode disabled\n.vlm-venv/bin/python scripts/eval_plot_vlm.py \\\n  --output artifacts/evaluation/qwen3-vl-plot-test\n```\n\nIf the client or SSH connection is interrupted, rerun the exact command with `--resume`. Completed\nrecord IDs are skipped; a truncated final JSONL line is repaired. Changing the model, subset,\nprepared records, prompt, plot, or decoding settings causes a manifest mismatch instead of silently\nmixing results.\n\nFor an unattended remote run that must wait for the OpenTSLM post-evaluation to release the GPU, use\n`scripts/run_qwen_plot_benchmark.sh`. It defaults to port 8001, records atomic lifecycle status in\n`qwen3-vl-benchmark-status.json`, resumes a partial evaluation, and shuts down its vLLM server when\nthe benchmark finishes.\n\nW\u0026B receives progress metrics and a class-balanced `test/examples` table containing the rendered plot,\ntarget JSON, raw response, parsed prediction, per-task correctness/errors, and latency. `metrics.json` uses the same\n`evaluate_rows` metric names as the trained model and deterministic feature baseline.\n\nRun the train-fitted transparent signal baseline and the train-prior constant baseline on those same\n512 record IDs with:\n\n```bash\nrobot-observe baseline \\\n  --prepared-root data/prepared/v1 \\\n  --output-root artifacts/baseline/signal-features-512 \\\n  --limit 512 --selection-seed 20260912 \\\n  --wandb-project robot-observability\n```\n\nThe output directory contains separate deterministic-signal and trivial-prior metrics plus the locked\nrecord manifest. It refuses to overwrite an existing result.\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nPROJECT_ROOT=${PROJECT_ROOT:-\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")/..\" \u0026\u0026 pwd)\"}\nPREPARED_ROOT=${PREPARED_ROOT:-\"${PROJECT_ROOT}/data/prepared/v1\"}\nOUTPUT_ROOT=${OUTPUT_ROOT:-\"${PROJECT_ROOT}/artifacts/evaluation/qwen3-vl-4b-one-shot\"}\nPYTHON_BIN=${PYTHON_BIN:-\"${PROJECT_ROOT}/.venv/bin/python\"}\nVLLM_BIN=${VLLM_BIN:-\"${PROJECT_ROOT}/.vlm-venv/bin/vllm\"}\nMODEL=${MODEL:-\"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct\"}\nPORT=${PORT:-8010}\nPOLL_SECONDS=${POLL_SECONDS:-60}\nIDLE_CONFIRMATIONS=${IDLE_CONFIRMATIONS:-2}\nLIMIT=${LIMIT:-512}\nLOG_ROOT=${LOG_ROOT:-\"${PROJECT_ROOT}/runs/qwen3-vl-one-shot-launcher\"}\n\n# vLLM can invoke sibling build tools (for example, ninja during FlashInfer JIT\n# warmup). An absolute VLLM_BIN alone does not place those tools on PATH.\nexport PATH=\"$(dirname \"${VLLM_BIN}\"):${PATH}\"\n\nmkdir -p \"${LOG_ROOT}\" \"$(dirname \"${OUTPUT_ROOT}\")\"\nLOG_PATH=\"${LOG_ROOT}/launcher.log\"\nSERVER_LOG_PATH=\"${LOG_ROOT}/vllm.log\"\nLOCK_PATH=\"${LOG_ROOT}/launcher.lock\"\n\nexec 9\u003e\"${LOCK_PATH}\"\nif ! flock -n 9; then\n  printf 'A one-shot GPU watcher is already active.\\n' \u003e\u00262\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nlog() {\n  printf '%s %s\\n' \"$(date --iso-8601=seconds)\" \"$*\" | tee -a \"${LOG_PATH}\"\n}\n\nif [[ -e \"${OUTPUT_ROOT}\" ]]; then\n  log \"Refusing to overwrite existing output: ${OUTPUT_ROOT}\"\n  exit 1\nfi\nif [[ ! -x \"${PYTHON_BIN}\" || ! -x \"${VLLM_BIN}\" ]]; then\n  log \"Python or vLLM executable is missing.\"\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nidle_checks=0\nlog \"Waiting for ${IDLE_CONFIRMATIONS} consecutive idle GPU checks.\"\nwhile (( idle_checks \u003c IDLE_CONFIRMATIONS )); do\n  if nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps=pid --format=csv,noheader,nounits | grep -Eq '[0-9]'; then\n    idle_checks=0\n    log \"GPU busy; checking again in ${POLL_SECONDS}s.\"\n  else\n    idle_checks=$((idle_checks + 1))\n    log \"GPU idle check ${idle_checks}/${IDLE_CONFIRMATIONS}.\"\n  fi\n  if (( idle_checks \u003c IDLE_CONFIRMATIONS )); then\n    sleep \"${POLL_SECONDS}\"\n  fi\ndone\n\nlog \"Starting ${MODEL} on port ${PORT}.\"\n\"${VLLM_BIN}\" serve \"${MODEL}\" \\\n  --port \"${PORT}\" \\\n  --dtype bfloat16 \\\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.70 \\\n  --limit-mm-per-prompt '{\"image\":2}' \\\n  \u003e\"${SERVER_LOG_PATH}\" 2\u003e\u00261 \u0026\nserver_pid=$!\n\ncleanup() {\n  if kill -0 \"${server_pid}\" 2\u003e/dev/null; then\n    kill \"${server_pid}\"\n    wait \"${server_pid}\" || true\n  fi\n}\ntrap cleanup EXIT INT TERM\n\nfor _ in $(seq 1 120); do\n  if curl --fail --silent --max-time 3 \"http://127.0.0.1:${PORT}/v1/models\" \u003e/dev/null; then\n    log \"vLLM is ready; starting one-shot evaluation.\"\n    break\n  fi\n  if ! kill -0 \"${server_pid}\" 2\u003e/dev/null; then\n    log \"vLLM exited before becoming ready; inspect ${SERVER_LOG_PATH}.\"\n    exit 1\n  fi\n  sleep 10\ndone\n\nif ! curl --fail --silent --max-time 3 \"http://127.0.0.1:${PORT}/v1/models\" \u003e/dev/null; then\n  log \"Timed out waiting for vLLM readiness.\"\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nPYTHONPATH=\"${PROJECT_ROOT}/src\" \"${PYTHON_BIN}\" \"${PROJECT_ROOT}/scripts/eval_plot_vlm.py\" \\\n  --prepared-root \"${PREPARED_ROOT}\" \\\n  --output \"${OUTPUT_ROOT}\" \\\n  --endpoint \"http://127.0.0.1:${PORT}\" \\\n  --model \"${MODEL}\" \\\n  --limit \"${LIMIT}\" \\\n  --shots 1\n\nlog \"One-shot evaluation complete: ${OUTPUT_ROOT}/metrics.json\"\narchitecture: soft_prompt\nbase_model: meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B\nwarm_start: OpenTSLM/llama-3.2-1b-har-sp\nupstream_commit: 2968f4b891baab4307f7e9d0043e87677b593a30\nexperiment:\n  hypothesis: conversational_all_intent_curriculum_without_channel_permutation\n  comparison_run: llama-har-sp-timef-rationale-v5b\ntargets:\n  format: rationale_then_answer\n  rationale_source: deterministic_signal_pseudolabels_v1\nprecision: bfloat16\nbatch_size: 3\ngradient_accumulation_steps: 5\nepochs: 1\nearly_stopping_patience: 3\nmax_wall_time_hours: 5.1\ntraining:\n  max_examples: 8192\n  warmup_fraction: 0.03\n  joint_attribution_curriculum: true\n  balanced_joint_permutation: false\n  curriculum_intents: all\nlearning_rates:\n  encoder: 0.0002\n  projector: 0.0001\n  lora: 0.00002\nlora:\n  rank: 16\n  alpha: 32\n  dropout: 0.0\nfit_probe:\n  train_examples: 48\n  validation_examples: 48\n  batch_size: 3\n  validation_batch_size: 4\n  epochs: 40\nvalidation:\n  at_start: true\n  generation_selection: event_intent_stratified\n  every_steps: 50\n  every_epoch: true\n  batch_size: 4\n  loss_subset: 128\n  generation_subset: 84\n  zero_signal_subset: 12\n  examples_table_rows: 21\nobservability:\n  generation_at_start: false\n  tensorboard: true\n  jsonl: true\n  log_every_steps: 10\n  sample_generations_every_steps: 250\n  gpu_metrics_every_seconds: 10\n  training_probe:\n    enabled: true\n    every_steps: 200\n    generation_every_steps: 500\n    loss_subset: 64\n    generation_subset: 48\n    zero_signal_subset: 12\n    matched_validation_subset: 64\n    manifest_table_rows: 256\n    dataset_table_rows: 16\n    examples_table_rows: 8\n  wandb:\n    enabled: true\n    project: robot-observability\n    entity: null\n    log_adapter_artifact: true\ncheckpoint_selection:\n  enabled: true\n  joint_metric: strongest_joint_accuracy\n  joint_weight: 0.5\n  onset_weight: 0.5\n  gates:\n    first_pass/schema_exact_match: 0.95\n    first_pass/semantics_macro_f1: 0.90\n    first_pass/contact_f1: 0.95\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"content":[{"text":"Approved command prefix saved:\n- [\"ps\", \"aux\"]","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0997d-e625-7d50-89f5-595adc024fc0","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["permissions.approved_command_prefix_saved"],"create_time":1789281560.101697,"turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Please continue\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0997d-e76f-70e2-a341-50dceea05cbf","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789281560.43144,"turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa6451ce85487d2bec519f7c53a98fa","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"I’m continuing. The new repository guide says the submission is frozen by default, but your explicit request reopens model exploration. I’ll treat a FactoryBench run as an experiment with hard gates: it must use real temporal input, finish a held-out evaluation, and improve the story without replacing canary-v4 or disturbing the shared service.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa6451e57cc87d2976aa74a7bb706de","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_H5AASJEGIaHiw1azhWlAsbp5","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa6451f4bc887d2a672650a631f04c1","input":"const r = await Promise.allSettled([\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,240p' docs/PARALLEL_AGENT_BRIEFS.md\",workdir:\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:16000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh pr list --state open --json number,title,headRefName,author,url,updatedAt\",workdir:\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",yield_time_ms:30000,max_output_tokens:8000,sandbox_permissions:\"require_escalated\",justification:\"May I inspect current open PRs before deciding where the FactoryBench experiment should live?\",\"prefix_rule\":[\"gh\",\"pr\"]}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git fetch origin main \u0026\u0026 git log --oneline --decorate -8 origin/main\",workdir:\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",yield_time_ms:30000,max_output_tokens:6000,sandbox_permissions:\"require_escalated\",justification:\"May I fetch the latest main before mapping the training experiment?\",\"prefix_rule\":[\"git\",\"fetch\"]})\n]);\nfor (const x of r) text(x.status === \"fulfilled\" ? x.value.output : String(x.reason));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281562.838891,"turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_H5AASJEGIaHiw1azhWlAsbp5","id":"ctco_01a0997e-1910-7540-90cf-487046b243f9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281573.136088,"turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.7 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"# Trace: parallel agent onboarding\n\nUse a separate task and git worktree for each editing agent. Paste the shared\nintroduction followed by **one** workstream prompt. The current coordinating task\ncontinues the frontend simplification. These are prompts to start tasks yourself;\nwriting this file does not launch agents.\n\n## Shared introduction — paste into every task\n\n```text\nYou are contributing to Trace, the team's Aionic Labs × Agentic Systems Lab Temporal\nAI Challenge submission. Work autonomously within the assigned workstream. First\nread AGENTS.md and docs/PARALLEL_AGENT_BRIEFS.md. Run entire doctor, inspect git status,\nfetch origin/main, and inspect recent commits and open PRs. Keep Entire active.\nPreserve existing teammate and agent work. Use a separate codex/ branch/worktree;\ndo not make parallel edits in the coordinator's dirty checkout.\n\nGather context across the whole product before editing:\n- frontend/README.md and docs/FRONTEND_INTEGRATION.md for the user flow and API.\n- inference/README.md for serving, input shape, normalization and checkpoint identity.\n- model_training/README.md for data preparation, splits, baselines and training.\n- data_ingestion/README.md and HUMAN_MAPPING_DECISIONS.md for TimeNet and source mapping.\n- docs/submission/QWEN_BASELINE.md for the exact verified plot-VLM prompt and input.\n- docs/submission/README.md, docs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.md,\n  docs/submission/PILOT.md and docs/submission/UI_WALKTHROUGH.md for evidence and limits.\nRead additional component instructions before changing that component's contract.\nVerify the files and deployment state rather than assuming these notes are current.\n\nProduct: retrospective investigation of recorded KUKA joint-torque contact events.\nThe flow is replay -\u003e select interval -\u003e measurements + OpenTSLM -\u003e interpretation\n-\u003e inspect evidence -\u003e export investigation. Publisher annotations, deterministic\nmeasurements and generated predictions are different sources. The value hypothesis\nis less engineer debugging time; no user study has established the saving yet.\nAn AI classifier alone is not the product advantage: test whether the investigation\nworkflow helps an engineer find and verify useful evidence.\n\nThe deployed model is canary-v4, immutable at process startup, SHA-256\n8ff63b84ae5b64758f66b3e0527f4f225a04bb2b6b39193c806f58d94cec9f23.\nIt uses seven canonical joints, 1024 contiguous raw samples each, 1 kHz, a 1.024 s\nhalf-open interval, and training-only robust normalization. Do not substitute\nreduced overview data, silently resample, pad incomplete windows or change the\ncheckpoint automatically. Two API modes do not mean two independent models.\n\nThe archived comparison uses 512 windows from 67 held-out recordings. Signal-feature\nsemantics macro F1 .9880 exceeds OpenTSLM .8845; usable OpenTSLM summary rate is .7793.\nDo not claim model superiority. Test data and demo cases have already been inspected;\nuse validation for development and new recording groups for fresh confirmation.\nKeep archived results immutable. No live robot control, verified root-cause diagnosis,\nphysical collision prevention, invented exact 3D motion, or extra orchestration LLM\nwithout a concrete demonstrated need.\n\nThe coordinator owns the active frontend/3D/replay redesign. Do not edit frontend/\nor its walkthrough from another workstream. Respect the ownership in your task.\nInspect other agents' PRs read-only for compatibility. Put proposed cross-module\ncontract changes into your handoff instead of silently editing outside your scope.\nDo not interrupt shared GPU jobs or restart/promote the private inference service.\nDo not expose the service publicly, commit credentials, or publish/send private\nweights to a new destination.\n\nBefore editing, briefly state the concrete problem, current end-to-end behavior,\nand challenge requirement your work advances. Implement one bounded useful result,\nrun focused checks, inspect the diff, commit only your intended files, and open a\nfocused draft PR against current main. Do not merge or deploy it from the worker\nworkstream; the coordinator integrates changes in sequence. End with the outcome,\nmeasured evidence, exact commands/artifacts, limitations, changed contracts, PR link,\nand next action. Clearly separate completed work from proposals and blocked work.\n```\n\n## Agent 1 — model reliability and evaluation\n\nOwns `model_training/`. Read `inference/runtime.py` for compatibility, but propose\nruntime changes in the handoff instead of editing the data agent's serving path.\n\n```text\nYour workstream is OpenTSLM output reliability. Inspect the latest training commits,\nexisting validation artifacts and run state before choosing work; avoid duplicating\nan active teammate experiment. Identify the highest-value remaining cause of invalid\nor unusable structured outputs. Preserve the seven-joint/1024-sample input contract.\n\nImplement and verify a bounded validation-only improvement or evaluation that\nmeasures usable-answer coverage alongside contact, semantics, joint and timing\nquality. Compare against the current validation baseline on identical recording\ngroups; record configuration, seeds, split identities and artifact hashes. Count\ninvalid and missing answers explicitly. Do not repair a generation into an invented\ncorrect answer. Do not train or select hyperparameters against the test set or the\nthree UI examples. Preserve archived submission metrics.\n\nStart with existing artifacts and lightweight tests. Before any GPU work inspect\ncapacity and active jobs; do not provision resources, kill jobs or launch a competing\ntraining run. If capacity is unavailable, finish the reproducible evaluation/config\nand document the precise run command instead of claiming an experiment happened.\nDo not promote a new checkpoint. Deliver evidence and a candidate recommendation\nthat the coordinator can evaluate for a separate controlled release.\n```\n\n## Agent 2 — raw recordings and adapter coverage\n\nOwns `data_ingestion/` and, only if needed, recording catalogue/data endpoints in\n`inference/server.py` and their tests. Does not own model runtime, frontend or releases.\n\n```text\nYour workstream is raw-data coverage through the existing adapter. Inspect recent\nTimeNet and semantic-validator PRs first; preserve their merged behavior. Determine\nhow to serve exact historical 1-kHz windows beyond the small demo excerpts without\nloading all recordings into browser memory or weakening the inference input contract.\n\nImplement one reproducible build/load -\u003e recording metadata/annotations -\u003e raw-window\npath using available authorized source data. Preserve recording identity, timebase,\nseven-channel order, units and half-open intervals. Verify requested values against\noriginal raw arrays and reject missing/gapped input explicitly. Reduced overviews\nmust remain clearly marked as display data. Source annotations must not enter model\nprompts. Preserve compatibility with the current demo-cases, replay, signals/events,\nquery and input-receipt contracts; propose any necessary schema extension explicitly.\n\nDo not duplicate the dataset-scout or semantic-agent work, add broad web ingestion,\nor fetch private teammate files without appropriate existing access/authorization.\nUse local fixtures and clean environment validation where possible. Deliver focused\nadapter tests, source/artifact hashes, a reproducible command and a draft PR. Do not\ndeploy or restart the shared service; provide deployment and rollback instructions\nfor the coordinator after compatibility review.\n```\n\n## Agent 3 — business evidence and submission\n\nOwns `docs/submission/` except `UI_WALKTHROUGH.md` and existing raw evaluation/receipt\nartifacts. Read implementation freely; do not edit frontend or model code.\n\n```text\nYour workstream is the challenge submission and the business case. Audit the actual\nchallenge brief against the repository's current evidence. Build a concise gap list\nwhere each requirement links to a real artifact or reproducible command. Distinguish\nrepository presence, test verification, deployed behavior and demonstrated user value.\n\nSharpen a two-minute story: engineer faces a recorded contact event -\u003e locates the\ninterval -\u003e compares generated interpretation with measured signals -\u003e inspects\nresponsible joints -\u003e exports evidence. Explain what Trace contributes beyond a\nstandalone classifier and what is still unproven. Keep the model-vs-feature-baseline\ncomparison honest; use only the existing audited metrics, not an invented advantage.\n\nMake the existing timed engineer pilot runnable: concrete task, comparison condition,\nsuccess criteria, timing/error capture sheet and interpretation rules. Do not invent\nparticipants or results, contact people, or claim debugging-time savings. Prepare a\nreviewable submission/checkpoint handoff checklist with precise missing metadata,\nincluding the reported unknown backbone revision. Do not upload weights, send messages,\nor submit externally. Deliver useful local submission documents and a draft PR.\nCoordinate wording with the frontend workstream through a short handoff; its current\nwalkthrough is being changed, so do not independently rewrite it.\n```\n\n## Optional agent 4 — independent product critique (read-only)\n\nThis can be given to another model. No model-specific capabilities are assumed.\n\n```text\nReview Trace as a robotics engineer and a skeptical challenge judge. Read the shared\ncontext, then actually use the current UI if computer use is available. Do not edit\nfiles, run inference in parallel with another tester, or redesign independently.\nThe coordinator is actively changing the UI; state the commit/build you reviewed.\n\nTry to answer: What happened? Which interval and joints support the answer? What is\nmeasured, annotated or predicted? Can I inspect the robot and signals without losing\nmy investigation? What can I export? What does this save compared with raw plots and\na standalone AI answer? Identify any unsupported claim or misleading physical cue.\n\nReturn at most five prioritized findings, each with a reproduction, user consequence,\nand smallest proposed correction. Separate observed defects from taste and hypotheses.\nDo not praise aesthetics without showing task success. Review an actual saved\ninvestigation, including model identity, input count and evidence. Do not treat a\nthree-case demonstration as a model-quality benchmark. Finish with the strongest\nreason this product could be useful and the most important missing proof.\n```\n\n## Integration handoff\n\nWorkers report: branch/PR and base SHA; owned files changed; outcome; verification\ncommands and results; artifacts; API/config compatibility; limitations; dependencies;\nany deployment or checkpoint action still required. One coordinator reviews and\nintegrates PRs, reruns checks for affected boundaries, and serializes live inference\nverification. An independent critique is useful after a concrete UI build is ready.\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"[{\"author\":{\"id\":\"U_kgDOCR0RPA\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"sametd04\",\"name\":\"Samet Degirmenci\"},\"headRefName\":\"codex/final-demo-impact\",\"number\":26,\"title\":\"Focus the demo on the predicted incident onset\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-13T06:37:32Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet/pull/26\"}]\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"From https://github.com/ukafkasyali/ysamet\n * branch            main       -\u003e FETCH_HEAD\n6316dd0 (origin/main, origin/HEAD) Merge pull request #19 from ukafkasyali/codex/source-ingestion-integration\ne9139ee Merge pull request #23 from ukafkasyali/codex/incident-cohorts\n366935f Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into codex/source-ingestion-integration\na67a5bb fix: open imported records in replay\nc2f2ae0 (origin/codex/incident-cohorts, codex/incident-cohorts) Harden cross-run cohort eligibility\n45c7aa7 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into codex/incident-cohorts\ne817441 Merge pull request #25 from ukafkasyali/bugfix/bosch-onboarding-source-root\nb657fbd feat: serve imported records for replay\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa64527773487d2b189f5c6e48b99ca","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_3vwrOAGfx9Rp43qTZtpfyTA9","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa6452cb4f887d2a1a5f8cb30544fdf","input":"const r = await Promise.allSettled([\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=10 samet@89.169.110.3 nvidia-smi --query-gpu=name,memory.total,memory.used,utilization.gpu --format=csv,noheader\",workdir:\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",yield_time_ms:30000,max_output_tokens:3000,sandbox_permissions:\"require_escalated\",justification:\"May I inspect the shared Nebius GPU capacity before deciding whether to launch a training experiment?\",\"prefix_rule\":[\"ssh\",\"-o\",\"BatchMode=yes\"]}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=10 samet@89.169.110.3 pgrep -af 'train_opentslm|post_training|vllm|evaluate_opentslm'\",workdir:\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",yield_time_ms:30000,max_output_tokens:5000,sandbox_permissions:\"require_escalated\",justification:\"May I inspect active model jobs on the shared Nebius VM without changing them?\",\"prefix_rule\":[\"ssh\",\"-o\",\"BatchMode=yes\"]}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=10 samet@89.169.110.3 find /home/samet -maxdepth 5 -type f -name status.json -o -name post_training_status.json -o -name best_model.pt\",workdir:\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",yield_time_ms:30000,max_output_tokens:8000,sandbox_permissions:\"require_escalated\",justification:\"May I inventory accessible training artifacts on the Nebius VM before starting another run?\",\"prefix_rule\":[\"ssh\",\"-o\",\"BatchMode=yes\"]}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=10 samet@89.169.110.3 find /home/atakantopaloglu/ysamet-training/runs -maxdepth 2 -type f -name status.json -o -name post_training_status.json -o -name best_model.pt\",workdir:\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",yield_time_ms:30000,max_output_tokens:8000,sandbox_permissions:\"require_escalated\",justification:\"May I read the shared training artifact inventory on Nebius, if permissions allow, without modifying it?\",\"prefix_rule\":[\"ssh\",\"-o\",\"BatchMode=yes\"]})\n]);\nfor (const x of r) text(x.status === \"fulfilled\" ? x.value.output : String(x.reason));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281573.410115,"turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_3vwrOAGfx9Rp43qTZtpfyTA9","id":"ctco_01a0997e-5e1f-7442-9be0-4f78e1f97fe8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281590.815712,"turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.5 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3, 81559 MiB, 0 MiB, 0 %\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"bash: line 1: post_training: command not found\nbash: line 1: vllm: command not found\nbash: line 1: evaluate_opentslm: command not found\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"/home/samet/trace-candidates/llama-har-sp-canary-v4-20260912/post_training_status.json\n/home/samet/trace-candidates/llama-har-sp-canary-v4-20260912/best_model.pt\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"find: ‘/home/atakantopaloglu/ysamet-training/runs’: Permission denied\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa64538881c87d288569a4c7b739316","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_Ko85oBC0vb0wKJPOCmmf3Rsr","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa6453a3b9487d28bb4a46a9d5e9efc","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=10 samet@89.169.110.3 ps -eo pid,etimes,args\",workdir:\"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet\",yield_time_ms:30000,max_output_tokens:12000,sandbox_permissions:\"require_escalated\",justification:\"May I list Nebius processes to verify no shared training job is still active?\",\"prefix_rule\":[\"ssh\",\"-o\",\"BatchMode=yes\"]});\nconst lines = r.output.split(\"\\n\").filter(x =\u003e /train_opentslm|post_training|vllm|evaluate_opentslm|inference\\.server/.test(x));\ntext(lines.join(\"\\n\") || \"No matching training or inference processes.\");\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281591.109521,"turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_Ko85oBC0vb0wKJPOCmmf3Rsr","id":"ctco_01a0997e-801b-75e3-834a-005048b47a58","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281599.515819,"turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.7 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"  50941   45005 tmux new-session -d -s trace-inference exec env TRACE_MODEL_CONFIG=inference/kuka-sp-v2.config.json TRACE_DEVICE=cuda inference/.venv/bin/python -m inference.server \u003e\u003e inference/server.log 2\u003e\u00261\n 102485   28573 inference/.venv/bin/python -m inference.server","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa645418d9487d2b8c6c82e51d0b84f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29"},"summary":[{"text":"**Evaluating GPU state and training setup**\n\nIt’s interesting that the GPU is idle, but it looks like the inference might still be using the CPU, showing no CUDA loads right now. The tmux command indicates that CUDA is configured, but the GPU memory isn't loading anything. I should check if the health is ready and maybe confirm the current config. It seems there’s no training process running on the H100, so I need to consider how to handle the dataset for FactoryBench.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_Iw4Lx2vcPv8tytvNF9SvB6nk","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa64547481887d296b7210a689ecdf5","input":"const r = await tools.web__run({search_query:[\n  {q:\"site:github.com/Forgis-Labs/FactoryBench FactoryBench dataset README\"},\n  {q:\"site:huggingface.co/datasets/FactoryBench/FactoryBench FactoryBench dataset files\"},\n  {q:\"FactoryNet arXiv 2605.09081 official\"}\n],response_length:\"long\"}); text(JSON.stringify(r));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281599.783982,"turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_Iw4Lx2vcPv8tytvNF9SvB6nk","id":"ctco_01a0997e-a8f8-7b81-ae9d-0b0c578087a6","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789281609.9761,"turn_id":"01a0997d-e59a-7ed3-9008-5472efcdac29"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.3 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\"FactoryBench/README.md at main · Forgis-Labs/FactoryBench · GitHub (https://github.com/Forgis-Labs/FactoryBench/blob/main/README.md)\\nciteturn18search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Python library and CLI for evaluating language models on the FactoryBench benchmark of industrial-machine reasoning across four causal levels (state / intervention / counterfactual / decision).Dataset: `FactoryBench/FactoryBench` on the Hugging Face Hub.\\n\\nEdit and raw actions\\n\\n# factorybench\\n\\nPython library and CLI for evaluating language models on the FactoryBench benchmark of industrial-machine reasoning across four causal levels (state / intervention / counterfactual / decision). Dataset: `FactoryBench/FactoryBench` on the Hugging Face Hub.\\n\\nWhat's included: dataset loader, prompt renderer, deterministic scorer for Levels 1-3, opt-in LLM-as-judge ensemble for Level 4 (with cache + Fleiss' kappa), built-in OpenAI / Anthropic / DeepSeek adapters, cost preview, model comparison, and a CLI covering the full evaluate / export / score / compare workflow. See `CHANGELOG.md` for what's landed.\\n\\n## Install\\n    \\n    pip install -e .                       # base install (mock model only)\\n    pip install -e \\\".[openai]\\\"             # adds OpenAI / DeepSeek (gpt-*, deepseek-*)\\n    pip install -e \\\".[anthropic]\\\"          # adds Anthropic (claude-*)\\n    pip install -e \\\".[all]\\\"                # everything\\n    pip install -e \\\".[dev]\\\"                # pytest for running the test suite\\n\\nThe base install includes `tiktoken` for tiktoken-counted cost previews; if it ever fails to import (air-gapped environments, lazy BPE-download failure on first use), the library falls back to a `len(text) / 4` heuristic and surfaces that in the preview output.\\n\\nPython 3.10+.\\n\\n### Provider credentials\\n\\nSet whichever provider keys you need before running:\\n    \\n    # bash / zsh\\n    export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\\n    export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...\\n    export DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=...\\n    \\n    # PowerShell\\n    $env:OPENAI_API_KEY    = 'sk-...'\\n    $env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = 'sk-ant-...'\\n    $env:DEEPSEEK_API_KEY  = '...'\\n\\n`factorybench info` shows which providers are configured and prints the exact `export` / `$env:` line for any that are missing. The library reads keys from the environment only -- it does not auto-load `.env` files. If you keep keys in a `.env`, source it yourself (`source .env` in bash, or `python-dotenv` in your own scripts) before invoking `factorybench` -- this matches the behavior of the underlying OpenAI / Anthropic SDKs and avoids surprising configuration.\\n\\n## Quick start (Python)\\n    \\n    from factorybench import register_model, evaluate\\n    \\n    @register_model(\\\"dummy\\\")\\n    class Dummy:\\n        def predict(self, prompt: str) -\u003e str:\\n            return \\\"0\\\"\\n    \\n    result = evaluate(model=\\\"dummy\\\", level=\\\"L1\\\", max_items=20)\\n    print(result.score)\\n    print(result.by_level())\\n    print(result.by_answer_format())\\n    df = result.to_dataframe()\\n\\n`evaluate(...)` accepts:\\n\\n  * `model`: a registered model name, a built-in provider spec (`\\\"mock\\\"`, `\\\"gpt-5.1\\\"`, `\\\"claude-sonnet-4.6\\\"`, `\\\"deepseek-chat\\\"`, ...), or any object with `predict(prompt) -\u003e str` (optionally `predict_batch(prompts) -\u003e list[str]`).\\n  * `level`: `\\\"L1\\\" | \\\"L2\\\" | \\\"L3\\\" | \\\"all\\\"` (L4 is rejected — needs a judge ensemble).\\n  * `split`: `\\\"test\\\"` (default), `\\\"validation\\\"`, `\\\"train\\\"`, or `\\\"mini\\\"` (50 items per level).\\n  * `max_items`: cap per level (useful for smoke tests).\\n  * `progress`: show a tqdm bar (default `True`).\\n\\n## CLI\\n    \\n    factorybench info                                            # version, dataset revision, cache, providers, prices\\n    factorybench info --json                                     # machine-readable (paste into bug reports)\\n    factorybench cache stats                                     # judge cache size + age\\n    factorybench cache clear -y                                  # wipe the judge cache\\n    factorybench prices list                                     # bundled price table + version stamp\\n    factorybench prices source                                   # show where prices are loaded from\\n    factorybench list models                                     # registered + built-in\\n    factorybench list levels                                     # item counts per level\\n    factorybench list templates --level L2                       # templates within a level\\n    \\n    # online evaluation against a provider\\n    factorybench evaluate --model claude-sonnet-4.6 --split mini\\n    factorybench evaluate --model gpt-5.1 --level L2 --max-items 50\\n    factorybench evaluate --model mock --level all --split mini  # no API needed\\n    \\n    # user-registered model from a script file\\n    factorybench evaluate --model my-model --import ./my_models.py --split mini\\n    \\n    # offline workflow (run inference yourself)\\n    factorybench export --level L2 --output prompts.jsonl\\n    # ... run your model over prompts.jsonl, writing {item_id, prediction} JSONL ...\\n    factorybench score --predictions predictions.jsonl --level L2 --output scores.json\\n\\nBuilt-in provider specs map to:\\n\\nPattern  | Adapter  | Required env var\\n--- | --- | ---\\n`mock`  | Canned-response (no API)  | --\\n`gpt-*`  | OpenAI chat completions  | `OPENAI_API_KEY`\\n`claude-*`  | Anthropic Messages API  | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`\\n`deepseek-*`  | DeepSeek (OpenAI-compatible)  | `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`\\n\\n    factorybench evaluate --model my-model --level L4 --judges deepseek-v3.2\\n\\nThe CLI prechecks required env vars (`OPENAI_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`) before any call is made -- if a key is missing, it exits with a clean error naming exactly which variable to set.\\n\\nEach L4 item's votes and the aggregate (median) are preserved in the saved JSON, and the result reports inter-judge agreement (Fleiss' kappa):\\n    \\n    result.l4_items()       # ItemResults that went through the panel\\n    result.fleiss_kappa()   # agreement across all L4 items\\n    result.judge_mode()     # 'paper-default' | 'single-judge' | 'custom'\\n\\nJudge calls are cached at `~/.cache/factorybench/judges/`, keyed on `(item_id, prediction_hash, judge_model, rubric_version)`. Re-runs with the same predictions and judge set make zero new API calls.\\n\\nJudges run in parallel by default (one thread per judge in the panel, capped at 8). Override with `--judge-concurrency N` -- set `1` to force sequential, or raise it for very large ensembles. Each judge is a different provider, so they don't share rate limits and parallelism is a free ~3x speedup on the paper-default ensemble.\\n\\nBy default, `--level all` skips L4 unless `--judges` is also given.\\n\\n## Long-eval robustness\\n\\nThree flags meant for real (long, expensive) runs:\\n    \\n    # Run candidate-model predict() in parallel. API adapters are I/O-bound; threads\\n    # are the right tool. Order-preserving. Default 1 (sequential). Ignored when\\n    # the model defines predict_batch.\\n    factorybench evaluate --model gpt-5.1 --level all --concurrency 8\\n    \\n    # If a run crashes, restart it. --resume points at a Result JSON from a prior\\n    # run; items that were scored without a parse_error are reused verbatim, and only\\n    # the remaining items are sent to the model (and judges).\\n    factorybench evaluate --model gpt-5.1 --level L4 --judges paper-default \\\\\\n        --output results/my-run.json\\n    # ... crash midway ...\\n    factorybench evaluate --model gpt-5.1 --level L4 --judges paper-default \\\\\\n        --output results/my-run.json --resume results/my-run.json\\n    \\n    # Re-aggregate against a saved judge cache without paying for any new judge call.\\n    # Items missing a cached vote are reported with parse_error=\\\"judge_cache_miss\\\".\\n    factorybench evaluate --model my-model --level L4 --judges paper-default \\\\\\n        --judge-cache-only\\n\\nSame three options are available on the Python API:\\n    \\n    result = fb.evaluate(\\n        model=\\\"gpt-5.1\\\",\\n        level=\\\"L4\\\",\\n        judges=\\\"paper-default\\\",\\n        concurrency=8,\\n        resume_from=\\\"results/my-run.json\\\",\\n        judge_cache_only=False,\\n    )\\n\\n## Cost preview\\n\\nBefore kicking off a paid run, get an order-of-magnitude estimate:\\n    \\n    # Standalone preview (no API calls).\\n    factorybench cost --model claude-sonnet-4.6 --level L4 --judges paper-default\\n    \\n    # evaluate --dry-run: same preview, exits 0 without running.\\n    factorybench evaluate --model claude-sonnet-4.6 --level L4 \\\\\\n        --judges paper-default --dry-run\\n    \\n    # Any L4 run (or run with estimated total \u003e $1) auto-prompts. Skip with --yes\\n    # in CI / scripted runs.\\n    factorybench evaluate --model claude-sonnet-4.6 --level L4 --judges paper-default\\n    # \u003e Continue? [y/N]:\\n    \\n    factorybench evaluate --model claude-sonnet-4.6 --level L4 --judges paper-default --yes\\n\\nBundled price table. Ships as `factorybench/prices.json` with a version stamp. Inspect with `factorybench prices list`. Three override paths, in precedence order: `FB_PRICES` env var \u003e `~/.config/factorybench/prices.json` \u003e `set_price()` runtime calls \u003e the bundled JSON.\\n\\n### Actual cost after the run\\n\\nThe built-in OpenAI / Anthropic adapters report each call's real `response.usage` to `factorybench`. After the run, `Result.cost` carries the actual dollar total and `Result.tokens_used` shows the breakdown:\\n    \\n    result = evaluate(model=\\\"claude-sonnet-4.6\\\", level=\\\"L4\\\", judges=\\\"paper-default\\\", split=\\\"mini\\\")\\n    result.cost              # 1.4032 (real, not heuristic)\\n    result.tokens_used\\n    # {\\\"candidate\\\": {\\\"model\\\": \\\"claude-sonnet-4-6\\\", \\\"input_tokens\\\": ..., \\\"output_tokens\\\": ..., \\\"calls\\\": ...},\\n    #  \\\"judges\\\": {\\\"gpt-5.1\\\": {\\\"model\\\": \\\"gpt-5.1\\\", \\\"input_tokens\\\": ..., \\\"output_tokens\\\": ..., \\\"calls\\\": ...},\\n    #             \\\"claude-sonnet-4.6\\\": {...}, \\\"deepseek-v3.2\\\": {...}}}\\n\\nThe CLI summary prints both numbers side by side:\\n    \\n    `actual cost         : $1.4032  (estimate was $1.8200)\\n    `\\n\\nThis works for any adapter that implements `predict_with_usage(prompt) -\u003e (str, {\\\"input_tokens\\\": ..., \\\"output_tokens\\\": ..., \\\"model\\\": \\\"...\\\"})`. User-registered models that only implement plain `predict()` keep running and just report `cost: 0.0` (no spend tracked).\\n\\n## Comparing models\\n\\nAfter running several models on the same split, drop a model x level table into your paper:\\n    \\n    from factorybench import evaluate, compare\\n    \\n    results = {\\n        \\\"gpt-5.1\\\":            evaluate(model=\\\"gpt-5.1\\\",           split=\\\"mini\\\"),\\n        \\\"claude-sonnet-4.6\\\":  evaluate(model=\\\"claude-sonnet-4.6\\\", split=\\\"mini\\\"),\\n        \\\"my-model\\\":           evaluate(model=\\\"my-model\\\",          split=\\\"mini\\\"),\\n    }\\n    comp = compare(results)\\n    print(comp.to_markdown())                # paste into a draft\\n    print(comp.to_latex(booktabs=True))      # paste into LaTeX\\n    comp.to_dataframe()                      # long-form pandas\\n\\nBest-per-row is bolded automatically (`bold_best=False` to disable). Absent or unscored levels render as `--`. `compare()` also accepts a dict of `model_name -\u003e path-to-result.json` (loaded for you), or just an iterable of paths (column names come from file stems).\\n\\nFrom the CLI:\\n    \\n    factorybench compare results/m0.json results/m1.json results/m2.json\\n    factorybench compare results/*.json --format latex --output table.tex\\n    factorybench compare m0.json m1.json --name gpt-5.1 --name claude-sonnet-4.6\\n\\n## What's intentionally missing\\n\\n  * Leaderboard `submit` subcommand (needs a backend).\\n  * Auto-fetched price table; the bundled snapshot is updated by hand. Use `set_price()`, `FB_PRICES`, or drop a file at `~/.config/factorybench/prices.json` to override.\\n  * Heatmap renderer on `Comparison` -- markdown/latex/json cover the paper use case.\\n  * Prompt caching on the Anthropic adapter -- each FactoryBench item has a unique time-series body, and the shared prefix per level (description + acronym mapping) is well below the 2K / 4K minimum cacheable prefix on Sonnet / Opus. Adding `cache_control` here would write entries that are never read.\\n\\n## Contributing\\n\\nSee CONTRIBUTING.md for dev setup, testing, and the bar for PRs. Bug reports should include the output of `factorybench info --json`.\\n\\n## Citation\\n\\nIf you use FactoryBench in academic work, please cite the paper:\\n    \\n    @article{factorybench2026,\\n      title   = {FactoryBench: Evaluating Industrial Machine Understanding},\\n      author  = {Merzouki, Yanis and Izquierdo, Coral and Ignuta-Ciuncanu, Matei and G{\\\\'o}mez-Bracamonte, Marcos and Maggioni, Riccardo and Lombardi, Alessandro and Mazzoleni, Camilla and Martelli, Federico and G{\\\\\\\"u}nther, Bal{\\\\'a}zs and Petersen, Jonas and Petersen, Philipp},\\n      journal = {arXiv preprint arXiv:2605.07675},\\n      year    = {2026}\\n    }\\n\\n## License\\n\\nLicensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Non-commercial use only.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nFactoryNet: A Large-Scale Dataset toward Industrial Time-Series Foundation Models (https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.09081)\\nciteturn18academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Title: FactoryNet: A Large-Scale Dataset toward Industrial Time-Series Foundation Models\\nTitle: FactoryNet: A Large-Scale Dataset toward Industrial Time-Series Foundation Models\\nAuthors: Karim Othman, Jonas Petersen, Matei Ignuta-Ciuncanu, Camilla Mazzoleni, Federico Martelli, Alessandro Lombardi, Riccardo Maggioni, Philipp Petersen\\nDate: Sat May  9 17:45:36 2026\\n\\nWe introduce the first universal pretraining corpus for industrial time-series data: FactoryNet. 51M datapoints across 23k end-to-end task executions (13.3k real, 9.8k synthetic) on six embodiments, unified by a shared schema that enables robust zero-shot cross-embodiment transfer and highly parameter-efficient anomaly detection. We introduce a novel schema: Setpoint, Effort, Feedback, Context (S-E-F-C) underlying the whole pipeline that maps any actuated system into a common representational frame. The corpus spans 27 annotated anomaly types alongside healthy baselines and counterfactual pairs across robotic manipulation and machining domains. Cross-embodiment transfer experiments yield positive results: under bias-aware metrics our model demonstrates fair cross-embodiment transfer capabilities on the evaluated source-target pair, while 24 schema-aligned signals achieves competitive anomaly detection performance compared to high-dimensional baselines. We release FactoryNet as a growing, multi-embodiment dataset to drive progress toward industrial foundation models.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nREADME.md · FactoryBench/FactoryBench at main (https://huggingface.co/datasets/FactoryBench/FactoryBench/blob/main/README.md)\\nciteturn18search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week;     url = \\\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/FactoryBench/FactoryBench/resolve/main/knowledge_graph/knowledge_graph.json\\\" ... If you use FactoryBench, please cite the dataset and the two upstream open-source datasets it incorporates (AURSAD and voraus-AD):\\n\\n# Datasets:\\n\\n* * *\\n\\nFactoryBench\\n\\n/\\n\\nFactoryBench\\n\\nlike [Button: 2]\\n\\nTasks: Question Answering Time Series Forecasting\\n\\nLanguages: English\\n\\nSize: 10K\u003cn\u003c100K\\n\\nArXiv:\\n\\narxiv: 2202.03211\\n\\narxiv: 2311.04153\\n\\nTags: robotics industrial time-series causal-reasoning benchmark machine-understanding\\n\\nLicense:\\n\\ncc-by-4.0\\n\\nDataset card Files xet Community\\n\\nmain\\n\\nFactoryBench / README.md\\n\\nImage: FactoryBench's picture\\n\\nFactoryBench\\n\\nREADME: correct license section to CC BY 4.0 (matches YAML frontmatter)\\n\\ne769902 verified\\n\\npreview code\\n\\n|\\n\\nRaw\\n\\nDownload with hf CLI\\n\\nCopy download link\\n\\nHistory Blame Contribute Delete\\n\\nSafe\\n\\n10 kB\\n\\nmetadata\\n    \\n    license: cc-by-4.0\\n    language:\\n      - en\\n    task_categories:\\n      - question-answering\\n      - time-series-forecasting\\n    tags:\\n      - robotics\\n      - industrial\\n      - time-series\\n      - causal-reasoning\\n      - benchmark\\n      - machine-understanding\\n    pretty_name: FactoryBench\\n    size_categories:\\n      - 10K\u003cn\u003c100K\\n    configs:\\n      - config_name: level_1\\n        data_files:\\n          - split: train\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_1/train.jsonl\\n          - split: validation\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_1/validation.jsonl\\n          - split: test\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_1/test.jsonl\\n      - config_name: level_2\\n        data_files:\\n          - split: train\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_2/train.jsonl\\n          - split: validation\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_2/validation.jsonl\\n          - split: test\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_2/test.jsonl\\n      - config_name: level_3\\n        data_files:\\n          - split: train\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_3/train.jsonl\\n          - split: validation\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_3/validation.jsonl\\n          - split: test\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_3/test.jsonl\\n      - config_name: level_4\\n        data_files:\\n          - split: train\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_4/train.jsonl\\n          - split: validation\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_4/validation.jsonl\\n          - split: test\\n            path: factorybench_qa/level_4/test.jsonl\\n    \\n\\n## Loading the data\\n    \\n    `from datasets import load_dataset\\n    \\n    # Load a single level/split\\n    ds = load_dataset(\\n        \\\"FactoryBench/FactoryBench\\\",\\n        data_files=\\\"factorybench_qa/level_1/test.jsonl\\\",\\n        split=\\\"train\\\",\\n    )\\n    \\n    # Load underlying telemetry\\n    import pandas as pd\\n    root = \\\"hf://datasets/FactoryBench/FactoryBench/factorywave\\\"\\n    episodes = pd.read_parquet(f\\\"{root}/episodes.parquet\\\")\\n    ur_125 = pd.read_parquet(f\\\"{root}/ur_signals.parquet\\\")\\n    ur_10  = pd.read_parquet(f\\\"{root}/ur_signals_10hz.parquet\\\")  # different episodes\\n    kuka   = pd.read_parquet(f\\\"{root}/kuka_signals.parquet\\\")\\n    screw  = pd.read_parquet(f\\\"{root}/ur_screwdriver_signals.parquet\\\")\\n    \\n    # Load the combined knowledge graph (machines, faults, error→protocol, ...)\\n    import json, urllib.request\\n    kg = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(\\n        \\\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/FactoryBench/FactoryBench/resolve/main/knowledge_graph/knowledge_graph.json\\\"\\n    ).read())\\n    `\\n\\n## Citation\\n\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nFactoryBench/FactoryBench_Sample · Datasets at Hugging Face (https://huggingface.co/datasets/FactoryBench/FactoryBench_Sample)\\nciteturn18search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; FactoryBench_Sample ...                     File \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/datasets/iterable_dataset.py\\\", line 2690, in __iter__\\n\\n# Datasets:\\n\\n* * *\\n\\nFactoryBench\\n\\n/\\n\\nFactoryBench_Sample\\n\\nlike [Button: 0]\\n\\nLicense:\\n\\nmit\\n\\nDataset card Files xet Community\\n\\nSplit (3)\\n\\ntrain\\n\\n[Select]\\n\\nThe dataset viewer is not available for this split.\\n\\nCannot load the dataset split (in streaming mode) to extract the first rows.\\n    \\n    Error code:   StreamingRowsError\\n    Exception:    CastError\\n    Message:      Couldn't cast\\n    id: string\\n    level: int64\\n    template_id: int64\\n    template_type: string\\n    hides: list\u003citem: null\u003e\\n      child 0, item: null\\n    question: string\\n    options: string\\n    answer: string\\n    root_cause: string\\n    acceptance_bounds: string\\n    provenance: string\\n    context: string\\n    to\\n    {'id': Value('string'), 'level': Value('int64'), 'template_id': Value('int64'), 'template_type': Value('string'), 'hides': List(Value('string')), 'question': Value('string')