{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:55:18.446Z","ordinal":15690,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa648d164f487d2a93dcc8061ba35f6","status":"completed","call_id":"call_l752vcqUF9qJ7TWS4EimZbHZ","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /private/tmp/ysamet-factorybench/model_training/docs/factorybench_canary.md\\n+# FactoryBench Level 1 canary\\n+\\n+This is an isolated cross-dataset feasibility experiment. It does not replace the\\n+KUKA canary-v4 checkpoint, its audited comparison, or the Trace demo.\\n+\\n+The source is `FactoryBench/FactoryBench` Level 1 at revision\\n+`2561c2c90560ae3df90ef8136f774faa5fb4b4e3`. The pinned JSONL has 15,321 items and\\n+SHA-256 `62a9fbacaf8f2ef82cc68145ca2c6b86a49327deb8f6d8fcd6c81efccee98c62`.\\n+The Hugging Face card labels the dataset CC BY 4.0. The separate GitHub tooling\\n+repository currently carries a different license; this experiment consumes the\\n+dataset file and does not copy its evaluation code.\\n+\\n+Rows cannot be split independently. Many questions reuse episodes and comparative\\n+questions connect two episodes. The adapter assigns whole connected episode\\n+components to deterministic 80/10/10 train, validation and sealed-test groups.\\n+It fits robust channel normalization on training rows only. Test rows are not\\n+evaluated during development.\\n+\\n+Run the source audit first:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+PYTHONPATH=src python scripts/audit_factorybench_l1.py /path/to/level_1.jsonl \\\\\\n+  --write-split-manifest /tmp/factorybench-audit-splits.json \\\\\\n+  --output /tmp/factorybench-audit.json\\n+```\\n+\\n+Then run the fit gate on an isolated H100 workspace:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+PYTHONPATH=src python scripts/train_factorybench_opentslm.py \\\\\\n+  --config configs/factorybench_l1_sp_canary.yaml \\\\\\n+  --data-file /path/to/level_1.jsonl \\\\\\n+  --output runs --run-name factorybench-fit-probe --fit-probe\\n+```\\n+\\n+Proceed to the full validation canary only if the 32-item probe reaches the configured\\n+training accuracy and changes its predictions when the signal is removed. The full\\n+run compares the untouched HAR warm start with the fine-tuned checkpoint on the same\\n+validation panel and records zero-signal and time-reversal ablations. Report this as\\n+cross-dataset transfer evidence only after the measured gates pass.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a09989-5963-7ac2-896e-62cf4245c0ce","create_time":1789282510.187604}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:55:18.486Z","ordinal":15691,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a09736-d5c6-7cc3-a099-0521c0b02bd2","turn_id":"01a09989-5963-7ac2-896e-62cf4245c0ce","session_id":"01a09736-d5c6-7cc3-a099-0521c0b02bd2","root_turn_id":"01a09989-5963-7ac2-896e-62cf4245c0ce","response_id":"resp_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa648cdf43887d2872d592d82697480","usage":{"input_tokens":191763,"cached_input_tokens":190626,"cache_write_input_tokens":1134,"output_tokens":715,"reasoning_output_tokens":124,"total_tokens":192478},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":3697431,"cached_input_tokens":3684578,"cache_write_input_tokens":12793,"output_tokens":7231,"reasoning_output_tokens":2057,"total_tokens":3704662},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":299692050,"cached_input_tokens":293063496,"cache_write_input_tokens":6504847,"output_tokens":744185,"reasoning_output_tokens":229871,"total_tokens":300436235}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:55:20.943Z","ordinal":15692,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09736-d5c6-7cc3-a099-0521c0b02bd2","turn_id":"01a09989-5963-7ac2-896e-62cf4245c0ce","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-44bf0e28-3df9-4087-84ab-dc64978820fd","changes":{"/private/tmp/ysamet-factorybench/model_training/docs/factorybench_canary.md":{"type":"add","content":"# FactoryBench Level 1 canary\n\nThis is an isolated cross-dataset feasibility experiment. It does not replace the\nKUKA canary-v4 checkpoint, its audited comparison, or the Trace demo.\n\nThe source is `FactoryBench/FactoryBench` Level 1 at revision\n`2561c2c90560ae3df90ef8136f774faa5fb4b4e3`. The pinned JSONL has 15,321 items and\nSHA-256 `62a9fbacaf8f2ef82cc68145ca2c6b86a49327deb8f6d8fcd6c81efccee98c62`.\nThe Hugging Face card labels the dataset CC BY 4.0. The separate GitHub tooling\nrepository currently carries a different license; this experiment consumes the\ndataset file and does not copy its evaluation code.\n\nRows cannot be split independently. Many questions reuse episodes and comparative\nquestions connect two episodes. The adapter assigns whole connected episode\ncomponents to deterministic 80/10/10 train, validation and sealed-test groups.\nIt fits robust channel normalization on training rows only. Test rows are not\nevaluated during development.\n\nRun the source audit first:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src python scripts/audit_factorybench_l1.py /path/to/level_1.jsonl \\\n  --write-split-manifest /tmp/factorybench-audit-splits.json \\\n  --output /tmp/factorybench-audit.json\n```\n\nThen run the fit gate on an isolated H100 workspace:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src python scripts/train_factorybench_opentslm.py \\\n  --config configs/factorybench_l1_sp_canary.yaml \\\n  --data-file /path/to/level_1.jsonl \\\n  --output runs --run-name factorybench-fit-probe --fit-probe\n```\n\nProceed to the full validation canary only if the 32-item probe reaches the configured\ntraining accuracy and changes its predictions when the signal is removed. The full\nrun compares the untouched HAR warm start with the fine-tuned checkpoint on the same\nvalidation panel and records zero-signal and time-reversal ablations. Report this as\ncross-dataset transfer evidence only after the measured gates pass.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /private/tmp/ysamet-factorybench/model_training/docs/factorybench_canary.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1789282518449,"completed_at_ms":1789282520943}}
